 average age of the directors is 62.2 years as of December 31, 2025. As of that date, in the absence of a specific provision in the      Articles of Association, ordinary law applied to the age of directors:      • the number of directors over the age of 70 may not exceed one third of the directors in accordance with the French Commercial Code        (Article L. 225-19, paragraph 2);      • the age limit for the Chairman is 65, under the French Commercial Code (Article L. 225-48).     86   Thales – 2025 Universal Registration Document                                                                                                                Governance and compensation                                                                                                                                 Composition of the Board of Directors    b) Independent directors                                                                  The Committee also considered that Mr. Loïc Rocard’s concurrent                                                                                           holding of an executive office within a public company is not likely According to its rules of procedure, the Board of Directors, based on                     to call into question his independence; a statement to this effect was the report of the Governance and Compensation Committee,                                  made to the Board by the representative of the French State. conducted its annual review of the situation of its members                               On this basis, the Committee considered that there was nothing to concerning the definition of and criteria for independent directors as                    compromise Mr. Rocard’s freedom of judgement in the performance of specified by the Afep-Medef code.                                                         his duties as a director of Thales and that there was therefore nothing The Board has decided to maintain the strict appro