      <data key="e_quote">BMW Group  SKIP TO MAIN CONTENT Company Innovation Responsibility &amp; Sustainability Investor Relations Insights Media Careers Company Leadership &amp; Governance Page Overview Search Contact BMW GROUP PROFILE. Page Overview Board of Management of BMW AG. Supervisory Board of BMW AG. Corporate Governance at the BMW Group. Board of Management of BMW AG. Dr. Milan Nedeljković Chairman of the Board of Management Dr.-Ing. Milan Nedeljković  Year/Place of birth: 1969, Krusevac (Serbia) Nationality: German, Serbian  Since 14 May 2026: Chairman of the Board of Management of BMW AG 2019 – 2026: Member of the Board of Management of BMW AG, Production 2018 – 2019: Senior Vice President Corporate Quality 2015 – 2018: Managing Director BMW Group Plant Munich 2013 – 2015: Managing Director BMW Group Plant Leipzig 2010 – 2013: Head of Assembly, BMW Group Plant Leipzig 2006 – 2010: Head of Paint Shop, MINI Plant Oxford 1999 – 2006: Various management positions at Plants Munich and Regensburg 1994 – 1999: Planning functions for bodyshop and press plant technologies 1993: Joined BMW AG as a trainee 2000 – 2004: Doctor of Engineering (Dr.-Ing.) at Chair of Metal Forming and Casting, Technical University of Munich 1988 – 1993: Studied Mechanical Engineering at RWTH Aachen University and Massachusetts Institute of Technology (Cambridge, USA) Dorothea von Boxberg People, Labour Relations Director Dorothea von Boxberg  Year of birth: 1974 Nationality: German  As of 01.09.2026: Member of the Board of Management of BMW AG, People, Labour Relations Director 2023 – 31.08.2026: Brussels Airlines SA/NV, Chief Executive Officer 2021 – 2023: Lufthansa Cargo AG, Chief Executive Officer and CFO 2018 – 2021: Lufthansa Cargo AG, Member of the Executive Board Product and Sales 2015 – 2018: Lufthansa Cargo AG, Vice President Global Sales Management 2007 – 2015: Deutsche Lufthansa AG, among other Head of Strategy and Subsidiaries 2005 – 2007: Star Alliance Services GmbH, Director Alliance Development 1999 – 2005: Boston Consulting Group 1993 – 1999: Combined studies of Electrical Engineering and business administration at TU Berlin and ESCP Paris Jochen Goller Customer, Brands, Sales Jochen Goller  Year/Place of birth: 1966, Miltenberg (Germany) Nationality: German  Since 1 November 2023: Member of the Board of Management of BMW AG, Customer, Brands, Sales 2018 – 2023: President and CEO of BMW Group Region China, Beijing 2015 – 2018: Head of Sales and Marketing BMW Brilliance Automotive, Beijing 2013 – 2015: Head of MINI 2009 – 2013: Head of Brand Management MINI UK and Ireland, Bracknell 2004 – 2009: Head of Marketing China, Beijing 2004: Head of Brand Communications MINI 1999 – 2004: Different functions in market communications 1999: Joined BMW Group 1990 – 1999: Different functions in events, brand marketing and sponsorship 1986–1989: Chemistry studies, University of Düsseldorf Dr. Nicolai Martin Purchasing and Supplier Network Dr. Nicolai Martin  Year/Place of birth: 1978, Frankfurt/Main (Germany) Nationality: German  Since 01 June 2025: Member of the Board of Management of BMW AG, Purchasing and Supplier Network Oct. 2024 – May 2025: Head of Product Line Luxury Class BMW, BMW ALPINA, Rolls-Royce Jan. 2024 – Sept. 2024: Head of Product Line Mid-Size and Luxury Class BMW, Rolls-Royce 2020 – 2023: Head of Automated Driving/Driving Experience 2019 – 2020: Head of Development Electric Drive Systems 2005 – 2010: Doctorate in Economics at the Technical University of Darmstadt (Volkswirtschaft – Institutionenökonomie) alongside full-time employment, Degree: Dr. rer. pol. 2004 – 2018: Various managerial positions within BMW AG, incl. in Development Driving Dynamics, Driver Assistance and General Vehicle Development 2004: Joined BMW AG, Development Driving Dynamics 1999 – 2004: Studied Industrial Engineering, specialising in Mechanical Engineering, at the Technical University of Darmstadt, Degree: Dipl.-Wirtsch.-Ing. Walter Mertl Finance Wa