dent Finance, Administration of Sales Region Americas (Woodcliff Lake, NJ, USA) 2021 – 2022: Vice President Assembly Plant Munich 2018 – 2020: Vice President Strategic Planning 2018: Head of Production Concept Midsize BMW 2015: Joined BMW AG, Head of Project Plant Development Mexico (San Luis Potosí, Mexico) 2006 – 2014: Worked in an international strategic consultancy, most recently as Partner 2002 – 2006: Research Associate at the Chair of Aeronautical Engineering of TU Munich; Doctorate in Engineering (Dr. Ing.) 1997 – 2002: Studied Aerospace Engineering at Technical University Munich; Degree: Dipl.-Ing. Supervisory Board of BMW AG. Dr. Nicolas Peter Chairman of the Supervisory Board of BMW AG. Dr. Nicolas Peter  Chairman of the Supervisory Board of BMW AG. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member and Chairman since 2025, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1962 Nationality: German, French  Since 2025: Chairman of the Supervisory Board of BMW AG Since 2025: Member of the Board of Directors and the Audit Committee of BNP Paribas S.A. Since 2023: Member of the Government Commission for the German Corporate Governance Code (GCGC) Since 2020: Chairman of the Board of Trustees of BMW Foundation Herbert Quandt 2023 – 2025: Member of the Board of Directors of FORVIA SE 2023 – 2025: Member of the Supervisory Board of KION Group AG 2017 – 2023: Member of the Board of Management of BMW AG, Finance 2011 – 2016: Head of Region Europe 2007 – 2011: Head of Group Controlling 2005 – 2007: Head of Sales Steering, Process Development and IT 2002 – 2004: Head of BMW Sweden 1999 – 2002: Managing Director Finance and Administration, BMW France 1996 – 1999: Department Head, Risk management, Corporate Finance 1993 – 1996: Treasurer, BMW Coordination Center, Belgium 1991 – 1993: Various management and project management functions 1991: Joined BMW AG 1988 – 1991: Completion of 2nd state legal examination 1989: Ph.D. (Dr. jur.) at the Ludwigs-Maximilians-Universität Munich 1984 – 1988: Studied law at the Ludwigs-Maximilians-Universität Munich, completion of 1st state legal examination  Status: 01/2026  Dr. Martin Kimmich Chairman of the General Works Council of BMW AG Dr. Martin Kimmich  Deputy Chairman of the Supervisory Board. Chairman of the General Works Council of BMW AG. Employee representative.  Mandate: Member and Deputy Chairman since 2023, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1972 Nationality: German  Since 2022: Chairman of the General Works Council of BMW AG Since 2022: Chairman of the Works Council Munich 2020 – 2022: Expert at the General Works Council of BMW AG 2019 – 2020: Union Secretary, IG Metall Bayern 2012 – 2018: Managing Director, IG Metall Munich 2006 – 2012: Political Secretary, IG Metall Munich 2003 – 2006: Ph.D. (Dr. jur.) at Martin-Luther-Universität Halle-Wittenberg 2000 – 2003: Referendariat (legal clerkship) at Kammergericht Berlin, degree: Zweite Juristische Staatsprüfung (second state examination in Law) 1994 – 2000: Law studies at Universität Hamburg, degree: Erste Juristische Staatsprüfung (first state examination in Law)  Status: 01/2026  Stefan Quandt Entrepreneur Stefan Quandt  Deputy Chairman of the Supervisory Board. Enrepreneur. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 1997, Deputy Chairman since 1999, elected until 2028 Year of birth: 1966 Nationality: German  Since 1996: Independent entrepreneur 1994 – 1996: Datacard, Marketing Manager Asia Pacific 1987 – 1993: Studies in Industrial Engineering at Technical University Karlsruhe (TH), degree: Diplom-Wirtschaftsingenieur (graduate industrial engineer)  Status: 01/2026  Stefan Schmid Chairman of the Works Council Dingolfing Stefan Schmid  Deputy Chairman of the Supervisory Board. Chairman of the BMW AG Works Council Dingolfing. Employee representative.  Mandate: Member since 2007, Deputy Chairman since 2008, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1965 Nationality: German  Since 2004: Deputy Chairman of the General Works Council of BMW AG and Chairman of the BMW AG Works Council Dingolfing Since 1995: Member of the BMW AG Works Council Dingolfing (full-time Member since 1998) 1985 – 1998: Electronics technician in car body manufacturing 1985: Joined BMW AG Apprenticeship power plant electronics technician and metal-working foreman  Status: 01/2026  Dr. Kurt Bock Chairman of the Supervisory Board of BASF SE Dr. Kurt Bock  Deputy Chairman of the Supervisory Board. Chairman of the Supervisory Board of BASF SE. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2018, Deputy Chairman since 2021, Chairman of the Audit Committee since 2020, elected until 2027 Year of birth: 1958 Nationality: German  Since 2020: Chairman of the Supervisory Board of BASF SE 2011 – 2018: Chairman of the Board of Executive Directors of BASF SE 2003 – 2011: Member of the Board of Executive Directors and CFO of BASF AG (BASF SE since 2008), since 2007 also Chairman and CEO of BASF Corporation (USA) 2000 – 2002: President of Logistics and Information Services, BASF AG 1998 – 2000: CFO of BASF Corporation (USA) 1996 – 1998: Managing Director, Robert Bosch Ltda. (Brazil) 1992 – 1996: Senior Vice President Finance and Accounting, Robert Bosch GmbH 1991 – 1992: Head of Technology, Director Planning and Controlling for Engineering Plastics, BASF AG 1985 – 1991: Various functions in the finance division of BASF AG 1985: Ph.D. (Dr. rer. pol.) at Universität Bonn 1977 – 1985: Studies in Business Administration at Westfälische Wilhelms-Universität Münster and Universität zu Köln as well as at Pennsylvania State University (USA)  Status: 01/2026  Ulrich Bauer Member of the Works Council Munich Ulrich Bauer  Member of the BMW AG Works Council Munich. Employee representative.  Mandate: Member since 2024, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1964 Nationality: German  Since 2014: Full-time Member of the BMW AG Works Council Munich 2012 – 2014: Head of Marketing, BMW Financial Services 2010 – 2012: Head of Marketing and Sales Services, BMW Bank GmbH 2001 – 2010: Head of Sales Management, BMW Bank GmbH; from 2007 also head of Business Line Retail 1998 – 2001: Head of European Sales Processes and Direct Banking, BMW Bank GmbH 1994 – 1998: Project manager at Roland Berger &amp; Partner 1992 – 1994: Trainee and Head of Operations Organization at Allianz Property Insurance, Stuttgart branch 1985 – 1990: Working student and freelancer at IBM Deutschland GmbH 1986 – 1991: Studies in Economics at Universität Hohenheim, degree: Dipl.-Oec. (graduate economist)  Status: 01/2026  Dr. Marc Bitzer Chairman and CEO of Whirlpool Corp. Dr. Marc Bitzer  Chairman and CEO of Whirlpool Corp. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2021, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1965 Nationality: German, US-American  Since 2017: Chairman and CEO of Whirlpool Corp. (USA) Since 1990: Co-Founder and Member of the Board of Directors of Simex Trading AG (Switzerland) 1999 – 2017: Various management positions at Whirlpool Corp. in Italy and North America 1991 – 1999: The Boston Consulting Group with assignments in Munich and Toronto (Canada), most recently as Vice President, Recruiting Director and member of the German Consumer Goods Practice Group 1984 – 1991: Studies in Economics and Ph.D. (Dr. oec.) at Universität St. Gallen (Switzerland)  Status: 01/2026  Dr. Christian Bruch CEO of Siemens Energy AG. Dr.-Ing. Christian Bruch  CEO of Siemens Energy AG. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2026, elected until 2030 Year of birth: 1970 Nationality: German  Since 2020: CEO, Siemens Energy AG Since 2020: CEO, Siemens Energy Management GmbH 2019 – 2020: Spokesperson of the Board of Management, Linde AG 2019 – 2020: Executive Vice President and CEO Linde Engineering, Linde plc (Ireland) 2015 – 2018: Member of the Board of Management, Linde AG (Engineering Division, corporate and support function Technology &amp; Innovation, Digitalisation) 2004 – 2015: Various management positions, Linde AG (Gases Division and Engineering Division) 2000 – 2004: Projekt engineer, RWE AG; from 2002 on: Head of Research and Project Development at RWE Fuel Cells GmbH 1997 – 2000: Research engineer at ETH Zurich (Switzerland); Ph.D. in engineering (Dr.-Ing.) 1991 – 1997: Studies in mechanical engineering at Leibniz Universität Hannover and the University of Strathclyde Glasgow (UK); degree: graduate engineer  Status: 05/2026  Rachel Empey Member of supervisory boards Rachel Empey  Member of supervisory boards. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2021, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1976 Nationalities: British, German  Since 2025: Member of the Supervisory Board and the Audit Committee of Deutsche Telekom AG (since 2026: Chairwoman of the Audit Committee) Since 2024: Member of the Foundation Board of Else Kröner-Fresenius-Stiftung Since 2023: Member of the Supervisory Board and the Audit Committee of ZF Friedrichshafen AG 2017 – 2022: CFO of Fresenius Management SE 2016 – 2021: Non-Executive Director and member of the Audit Committee of Inchcape plc (UK) 2011 – 2017: Member of the Management Board of Telefónica Deutschland Holding AG (Finance, Strategy and Innovation); Joint Leader of the Board, General Manager of Operating Business (2014) 2003 – 2011: Various positions in the Telefónica Group in the UK and Germany 2002 – 2003: Commercial Director, Weir Group plc (UK) 2000 – 2002: Business Analyst, Lucent Technologies (UK) 2000: Studies at the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales (ICAEW), degree: Chartered Accountant 1997 – 2000: Audit Executive at Ernst &amp; Young Ltd., Bristol (UK) 1994 ­­– 1997: Studies in Mathematics at the University of Oxford (UK)  Status: 04/2026  Dr. h.c. Susanne Klatten Entrepreneur Dr. h.c. Susanne Klatten  Entrepreneur. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 1997, elected until 2028 Year of birth: 1962 Nationality: German  Since 1991: Independent entrepreneur 1988: Studies at the International Institute for Management Development (Lausanne, Switzerland), degree: MBA 1984 – 1985: Business Studies at the University of Buckingham (UK), degree: B.Sc.  Status: 01/2026  Jens Köhler Chairman of the Works Council Leipzig Jens Köhler  Chairman of the BMW AG Works Council Leipzig. Employee representative.  Mandate: Member since 2021, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1964 Nationality: German  Since 2002: Chairman of the BMW AG Works Council Leipzig Since 1993: Member of the Works Council of the BMW branch Chemnitz (Chairman and thus permanent Member of the General Works Council of BMW AG since 1996) 2002: Relocation to BMW Group Plant Leipzig 1996 – 2001: Qualification and car mechanic master craftsman training 1991: Joined BMW AG (Chemnitz branch) Skilled worker training as motor mechanic/locksmith  Status: 01/2026  André Mandl Chairman of the Works Council Regensburg/Wackersdorf André Mandl  Chairman of the BMW AG Works Council Regensburg/Wackersdorf. Employee representative.  Mandate: Member since 2022, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1984 Nationality: German  Since 2021: Chairman of the BMW AG Works Council Regensburg/Wackersdorf 2018 – 2021: Full-time Member of the BMW AG Works Council Regensburg/Wackersdorf 2010 – 2018: Expert and Substitute Member of the BMW AG Works Council Regensburg/Wackersdorf 2004 – 2011: Production worker at BMW Group Plant Regensburg and further training as a mechanical engineer and technical economist (IHK – Chamber of Commerce and Industry) 2001 – 2004: Training as an industrial mechanic, BMW Group Plant Wackersdorf  Status: 01/2026  Dr. Dominique Mohabeer Member of the Works Council Munich Dr. rer. pol. Dominique Mohabeer  Member of the BMW AG Works Council Munich. Employee representative.  Mandate: Member since 2012, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1963 Nationality: German, Belgian  Since 2002: Member of the BMW AG Works Council Munich 2000: Joined BMW AG 1995 – 1999: Research assistant at the Institute of Occupational Science at Universität Kassel 1988 – 1995: Studies in Business Administration at Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München, degree: Diplom-Kauffrau (business graduate) 1985 – 1988: Studies in Sinology at Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München; interpreting school  Status: 01/2026  Horst Ott District manager of IG Metall Bayern Horst Ott  District manager of IG Metall Bayern. Employee representative.  Mandate: Member since 2024, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1966 Nationality: German  Since 2023: District manager of IG Metall Bayern 2012 – 2023: 1st representative of IG Metall Amberg and member of the Advisory Board of IG Metall 2008 – 2012: 2nd representative of IG Metall Amberg 1992 – 2008: Technical Secretary of IG Metall Amberg 1990 – 1991: Studies at the European Academy of Labour in Frankfurt a. M.: Labour Law, Economics and Social Law 1989 – 1990: Trainee at IG Metall Augsburg 1981 – 1989: Training as a machine fitter at RENK AG Augsburg; Worked as a repair fitter from 1983  Status: 01/2026  Dr. Mike Reichelt Head of Neue Klasse BMW Dr. Mike Reichelt  Head of Neue Klasse BMW. Employee representative (executive employee).  Mandate: Member since 2026, appointed until 2029 Year of birth: 1970 Nationality: German  Since 2020: Head of Neue Klasse BMW 2019 – 2020: Head of the mid-range product line; overall responsibility for the 2–6 Series, X3/X4 (incl. BEV) 2015 – 2019: Project lead for the further development of the rear-wheel-drive architecture (CLAR WE) of BMW AG 2009 – 2015: Head function for the technical concept of the rear-wheel-drive architecture (CLAR) and corresponding total vehicles 2001 – 2009: Various head functions within BMW AG, including head of the Structural Dynamics and Vibration department (Total Vehicle division) 1998 - 2003: Ph.D. (Dr.-Ing.) at Technische Universität Chemnitz 1996: Joined BMW AG in Munich, focus: body development (acoustics and vibration comfort) 1990 - 1995: Studies in Mechanical Engineering at Technische Universität Chemnitz, degree: Dipl.-Ing. (graduate engineer)  Status: 07/2026  An