                8     89%          3 100%       (a)   Since September 5, 2023, the French State has appointed its representative on the Board directly by decree, without seeking the approval of the Annual General Meeting of            shareholders (see Article 4-I paragraph 1 of Ordinance No. 2014-948). By decree dated January 29, 2024, Mr. Alexis Zajdenweber succeeded Mr. Emmanuel Moulin as            the State’s new representative on the Board of Directors.      (b)   Director(s) proposed by the State (Article 6 of Ordinance No. 2014-948).      (c)   Attendance is calculated based on the total number of meetings at which the director was in office, as the case may be, on the Board or the Committee concerned. The only            director who left office in 2025, namely Mr. Charles Edelstenne, left before the meetings were held.      (d)   Mr. Charles Edelstenne has resigned from his directorship with effect from January 9, 2025. On February 4, 2025, the Board of Directors co-opted Ms. Valérie Guillemet to            the Board for the remainder of his term, i.e. until the Annual General Meeting called in 2026 to approve the financial statements for the year ended December 31, 2025.            This co-optation was ratified by the Annual General Meeting of May 16, 2025.      (e)   Independence under the Afep-Medef code, confirmed by the Board of Directors on March 2, 2026.      (f)   Ms. Anne Rigail and Ms. Marie-Françoise Walbaum attend meetings of the Strategic &amp; CSR Committee for CSR-related agenda items, as well as meetings of the two other            Committees dealing with CSR issues.        •     Committees: Strategic and CSR (S&amp;C), Audit and Accounts (A&amp;A) and Governance &amp; Compensation (G&amp;C).            Status:          Member,          Chair.        At December 31, 2025, the Board of Directors comprised a single executive member, namely the Chairman and Chief Executive Officer,      Mr. Patrice Caine, and 15 non-executive members.      The average age of the directors is 62.2 years as of December 31, 2025. As of that date, in the absence of a specific provision in the      Articles of Association, ordinary law applied to the age of directors:      • the number of directors over the age of 70 may not exceed one third of the directors in accordance with the French Commercial Code        (Article L. 225-19, paragraph 2);      • the age limit for the Chairman is 65, under the French Commercial Code (Article L. 225-48).     86   Thales – 2025 Universal Registration Document                                                                                                                Governance and compensation                                                                                                                                 Composition of the Board of Directors    b) Independent directors                                                                  The Committee also considered that Mr. Loïc Rocard’s concurrent                                                                                           holding of an executive office within a public company is not likely According to its rules of procedure, the Board of Directors, based on                     to call into question his independence; a statement to this effect was the report of the Governance and Compensation Committee,                                  made to the Board by the representative of the French State. conducted its annual review of the situation of its members                               On this basis, the Committee considered that there was nothing to concerning the definition of and criteria for independent directors as                    compromise Mr. Rocard’s freedom of judgement in the performance of specified by the Afep-Medef code.                                                         his duties as a director of Thales and that there was therefore nothing The Board has decided to maintain the strict approach adopted in                          to prevent the Board from declaring him an independent director. previous years: directors appointed by the Annual General Meeting                         With regard to Ms. Ruby McGregor-Smith, the Committee noted that on the proposal of a shareholder (“Public Sector” or “Industrial Partner”)                the sales generated with Thales by the Atkins Realis group, of which or a category of shareholders (employees), or appointed by trade                          she is a director of the Canadian parent company, represent less unions may not be considered independent within the meaning of the                        than 1% of the sales of the two groups. Afep-Medef code. Under these conditions, only the four “External                                                                                                                       —                                                                                                                                                                                        — directors” according to the terms of the shareholders’ agreement (out of                  Lastly, the Committee examined the situation of Ms. Anne-Claire                              — a total of 16 directors) can be declared independent.                                     Taittinger, the fourth “external director”, in view of the fact that she                                                                                           has been a director of the Company for more than 12 years, and At its meeting of February 20, 2026, the Governance and                                   this since the Annual General Meeting of May 15, 2024. It Compensation Committee carefully studied the responses to the detailed                    recommended that the Board maintain this status, based in particular questionnaire sent to each of these “External directors” in January 2026.                 on the following reasons alr