Seniority on the Board                         In September 2011, he was appointed Managing Director for Economic and Social Affairs                                                      at Dassault Aviation.       16.6 years                                                      In January 2013, he became Deputy CEO of Dassault Aviation.       Current term expires       2026 AGM                                       He is a member of the Management Committee of Dassault Aviation.        Number of shares held                          He is an Officier de l’Ordre National du Mérite [Officer of the National Order of Merit] and       509 Thales shares                              a Chevalier de l’Ordre National de la Légion d’honneur [Knight of the National Order of the                                                      Legion of Honor].                                                       List of offices and other positions in French and foreign companies                                                      Positions held in other companies                                                      In France: Deputy CEO of Dassault Aviation (1), Vice-Chairman of GIFAS, member of the                                                      Advisory Board of Daher Industrial Services SAS.                                                      Abroad: Director of Dassault Falcon Jet Corporation (USA) and of SITAM Belgium SA.                                                      Other positions held by Mr. Segalen over the last five years                                                      In France: none.                                                      Abroad: Director and member of the Audit Committee of Sabca (1).      (1)   Listed company.     96   Thales – 2025 Universal Registration Document                                                                        Governance and compensation                                                                                     Composition of the Board of Directors     ANNE-CLAIRE TAITTINGER   (age 76)                    Born on November 3, 1949, Anne-Claire Taittinger is a French national and a graduate of                              the Institut d’Études Politiques de Paris. She holds a master’s degree in urban sociology, a  Independent director        graduate degree in urban planning, and an MBA from HEC (CPA). She began her career in                              1976 in the Caisse des Dépôts et Consignations group as head of urban planning  Chairwoman of the Audit     operations at the Société centrale d’équipement du territoire.  and Accounts Committee                              In 1979, she joined the Louvre Group as the Company Secretary and then became  Date of first appointment   Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Compagnie Financière Deville. She successively                              served as Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Compagnie Financière Leblanc and of  May 15, 2012                Elm-Leblanc, Vice-Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of the Deville industrial group,  Seniority on the Board      Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Parfums Annick Goutal France USA, and then  13.6 years                              Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Baccarat.                                                     —                                                                                                                                    —  Current term expires                              She became CEO and then Chairman of Société du Louvre in 1997. In 2002, she was                       —                              named Chairwoman of Groupe Taittinger as well as CEO of its subsidiary Groupe du Louvre  2026 AG                     in the context of a separation of the roles of Chairman and CEO. She stepped down as a  Number of shares held       Chief Executive Officer in July 2006, after having managed the sale of the Taittinger group                              to an investment fund in 2005.  612 Thales shares                              Since September 2006, Anne-Claire Taittinger has been part of the pool investors acquiring            |1|                              Champagne Taittinger.                              She became involved in the Women’s Forum for the Economy and Society in 2004, where                              she was a co-founder and an investor.                               List of offices and other positions in French and foreign companies                                   |2|                              Positions held in other companies                              In France: Chairman of SAS Le Riffray, member of the Board of Directors of Société des                              Amis du Louvre.                              Abroad: none.                              Other positions held by Ms. Taittinger over the past five years                                       |3|                              In France: until July 2018: Director and member of the Nomination and Compensation                              Committees of Carrefour (1). Until 2022: Member of the Management Committee of SAS                              E-Attestation.                              Abroad: none. (1)   Listed company.                                                                                                                                    |4|                                                                                                                                       |5|                                                                                                                                       |6|                                                                                                                                       |7|                                                                                                                                       |8|                                                                                   2025 Universal Registration Document – Thales   97 4      Governance and compensation      Composition of the Board of Directors          ÉRIC TRAPPIER        (age 65)                                       Born on June 1, 1960, Éric Trappier is a French national and a graduate of the École Sud                                                      Telecom (formerly known as the Institut National Telecom).       Director proposed                                                      He began his career in 1984 at the Technical Division of Dassault Aviation (responsible for       by the Industrial Partner                                                      the development of ATL2 and Mirage 2000 systems).       Member of the Strategy                         In 1991, he became responsible for sales in India and Asia, and then the United Arab       &amp; CSR Committee                                Emirates in 1996.        Date of first appointment                      He was named Director of the Middle East and Africa region in 2000, Director of Military       May 19, 2009                                   Exports in 2001, and Senior International Vice President in 2002.        Seniority on the Board                         In 2006, Éric Trappier was appointed Executive Vice President of Dassault Aviation.       16.6 years                                     He was appointed Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Dassault Aviation in January 2013.       Current term expires                           He is an Officier de l’Ordre National de la Légion d’honneur [Officer of the National Order       2026 AGM                                       of the Legion of Honor] and a Chevalier de l’Ordre National du Mérite [Knight of the                                                      National Order of Merit]. In 2022, he was awarded the Aeronautics medal.       Number of shares held       500 Thales shares                              On January 9, 2025, Mr. Éric Trappier became Chairman of Groupe Industriel Marcel Dassault.                                                       List of offices and other positions in French and foreign companies                                                      Positions held in other companies                                                      In France: Chairman of Groupe Industriel Marcel Dassault (GIMD), Chairman and Chief                                                      Executive Officer of Dassault Aviation (1), Chairman of the UIMM, Honorary Chairman of                                                      GIFAS. Member then Executive Committee member of the Conseil National de l’Industrie,                                                      Director and Chairman of the Figaro SASU Group, Chairman of Figaro SAS, Chairman of                                                      Rond Point Immobilier SAS, Permanent Representative of GIMD on the Board of Directors (as                                                      Director and Chairman) of Dassault Medias SAS, Representative of GIMD (Chief Executive                                                      Officer) at Dassault Wine Estates SAS and Representative of GIMD (Chairman) at Rond Point                                                      Investissements SAS.                                                      Abroad: Chairman of Dassault Falcon Jet Corporation (USA), member of the Board of                                                      Directors of ASD Belgium (European Association of Aerospace and Defence Industries),                                                      Permanent Representative of GIMD on the Board of Directors (as Managing Director and                                                      Chairman) of Sitam Belgique SA (Belgium) and director of Dasbat Aviation LLC (UAE).                                                      Other positions held by Mr. Trappier over the last five years                                                      In France: Director of Sogitec Industries (France), President of GIFAS, President of Cidef.                                                      Abroad: Chairman of the Defence Committee then Chairman of the ASD (Belgium).                                                      Chairman and Director of Dassault Reliance Aerospace Limited (DRAL) (India).      (1)   Listed company.           MARIE-FRANÇOISE WALBAUM        (age 75)                                       Born on March 18, 1950, Marie-Françoise Walbaum is a French national and holds                                                      degrees in economics and sociology from the Université Paris X.       Director proposed                                                      She began her career in 1973 at BNP Paribas, where she held various retail banking and       by the Industrial Partner                                                      credit analysis positions until 1981. From 1981 to 1994, she successively held the positions       Date of first appointment                      of Project Leader at the General Inspection Department of BNP, CEO of SICAV, and CEO of                                                      the brokerage firm Patrick Dubouzet S.A. In 1994, she became head of listed and unlisted       September 17, 2013                             investments and the private equity portfolio at BNP Paribas, a company she left in the       Seniority on the Board                         summer of 2012 after 39 years of service. Since then, Marie-Françoise Walbaum has held                                                      directorships in a number of companies in addition to Thales, including ESSO, Peugeot       12.5 years                                     Invest, Imerys and Isatis.       Current term expires       2026 AGM                                       List of offices and other positions in French and foreign companies                                                      Positions held in other companies       Number of shares held       500 Thales shares                              In France: none.                                                      Abroad: none.                                                      Other positions held by Ms. Walbaum over the past five years                                                      In France: independent director of FFP – now Peugeot Invest (1) – (and Chair of the Finance                                                      and Audit Committee and Member of the Governance, Appointments and Compensation                                                      Committee) until the Annual General Meeting of May 24, 2024 and of Imerys (1) (and Chair                                                      of the Appointments Committee and the Compensation Committee) until the Annual General                                                      Meeting of May 10, 2024 and independent director of Esso (1) (and Chair of the Audit                                                      Committee) until March 18, 2020. Member of the Supervisory Board of Isatis Capital until                                                      March 18, 2025.                                                      Abroad: none.      (1)   Listed company.     98   Thales – 2025 Universal Registration Document                                                                                                            Governance and compensation                                                                                                                            Composition of the Board of Directors     ALEXIS ZAJDENWEBER   (age 49)                                                A graduate of the Institut d’études politiques de Paris and the École nationale                                                          d’administration, Alexis Zajdenweber began his career in 2003 with the French Ministry of  State representative (appointed by order                the Economy, Finance and Industry, as deputy head of the Savings and Financial Markets  of January 29, 2024), director proposed                 office of the Treasury department where he became deputy head of the Corporate Financing  by the Public Sector                                    and Development Office in 2006.  (Article 4 of Ordinance No. 2014-948)                   In 2007, he was seconded to the Economic, Financial and Monetary Affairs Department of                                                          France’s Permanent Representation to the European Union in Brussels as an advisor on  Member of the Strategy                                  competition and state aid, company law and corporate governance.  &amp; CSR Committee                                                          Alexis Zajdenweber returned to the French Treasury in 2009 as Head of the Banking and  Member of the Governance                                Payment Services Office. In 2011, he was appointed Head of the Investment, Anti-Financial  and Compensation Committee                              Crime and Sanctions Office.                                                                                            —                                                                                                                                                                                 —                                                                                                                                                                                 —  Date of first appointment                               In 2012, he was appointed Financial Sector Advisor to the Minister of the Economy and Finance.  as State representative                                                          He joined Agence des Participations de l’État in 2014 as