e building  aspect – fire-resistant glazing and partitions, acoustic  ceiling and partition solutions, lightweight ventilated  façade systems, solar-control glazing, waterproofing  systems for flat roofs, or technical flooring for heavy- traffic areas – and the infrastructure aspect –  fiberglass for reinforcing runways and taxiways,  concrete admixtures, waterproofing solutions for  bridges and underground passages, and fireproofing  for steel structures.  PRESENTING SAINT-GOBAIN SAINT-GOBAIN TODAY 32 SAINT-GOBAIN • UNIVERSAL REGISTRATION DOCUMENT 2025 Ë www.saint-gobain.com Ventilation duct  insulation “Cool roof”  waterproofing Highly energy-efficient  glazing Electrochromic  insulating glass Fire-resistant glass  partitions High-security glass Glass wool insulation Mortars for floor  covering Acoustic ceilings Perforated  plasterboard Low-carbon concrete Example: Saint-Gobain transport infrastructure solutions  PRESENTING SAINT-GOBAIN SAINT-GOBAIN TODAY SAINT-GOBAIN • UNIVERSAL REGISTRATION DOCUMENT 2025 33 Injections  for concrete repair Structural bonding Solutions for  low-carbon concrete Solar control glazing Impact-resistant  partitions Acoustic  plasterboard Fire protection  for structures Structural reinforcement  of taxiways Flooring Waterproofing solutions  for bridge decks In-transit concrete  quality control Protective coatings  for concrete Repair mortars for concrete  finishing and grouting Fiberglass  reinforcement veil Structural sealing  for concrete works Pipes  B – Industrial markets Country by country, Saint-Gobain deploys this same  solutions-based approach over its industrial application  lines. In a context marked by the energy transition,  decarbonization, and the search for performance, the  Group’s solutions make it possible to support the major  industrial players in their transformation. Saint-Gobain  is positioned as a key technological partner, offering high  value-added materials and systems. The Group offers a  comprehensive range 