 Administration at Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München, degree: Diplom-Kauffrau (business graduate) 1985 – 1988: Studies in Sinology at Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München; interpreting school  Status: 01/2026  Horst Ott District manager of IG Metall Bayern Horst Ott  District manager of IG Metall Bayern. Employee representative.  Mandate: Member since 2024, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1966 Nationality: German  Since 2023: District manager of IG Metall Bayern 2012 – 2023: 1st representative of IG Metall Amberg and member of the Advisory Board of IG Metall 2008 – 2012: 2nd representative of IG Metall Amberg 1992 – 2008: Technical Secretary of IG Metall Amberg 1990 – 1991: Studies at the European Academy of Labour in Frankfurt a. M.: Labour Law, Economics and Social Law 1989 – 1990: Trainee at IG Metall Augsburg 1981 – 1989: Training as a machine fitter at RENK AG Augsburg; Worked as a repair fitter from 1983  Status: 01/2026  Dr. Mike Reichelt Head of Neue Klasse BMW Dr. Mike Reichelt  Head of Neue Klasse BMW. Employee representative (executive employee).  Mandate: Member since 2026, appointed until 2029 Year of birth: 1970 Nationality: German  Since 2020: Head of Neue Klasse BMW 2019 – 2020: Head of the mid-range product line; overall responsibility for the 2–6 Series, X3/X4 (incl. BEV) 2015 – 2019: Project lead for the further development of the rear-wheel-drive architecture (CLAR WE) of BMW AG 2009 – 2015: Head function for the technical concept of the rear-wheel-drive architecture (CLAR) and corresponding total vehicles 2001 – 2009: Various head functions within BMW AG, including head of the Structural Dynamics and Vibration department (Total Vehicle division) 1998 - 2003: Ph.D. (Dr.-Ing.) at Technische Universität Chemnitz 1996: Joined BMW AG in Munich, focus: body development (acoustics and vibration comfort) 1990 - 1995: Studies in Mechanical Engineering at Technische Universität Chemnitz, degree: Dipl.-Ing. (graduate engineer)  Status: 07/2026  Anke Schäferkordt Member of supervisory boards Anke Schäferkordt  Member of supervisory boards. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2020, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1962 Nationality: German  Since 2019: Member of the Supervisory Board of Serviceplan Group Management SE 2019 – 2025: Non-executive director and member of the Audit Committee of Wayfair Inc. (Boston, USA) 2010 – 2022: Member of the Supervisory Board of BASF SE (2020 – 2022: member of the Audit Committee) 2012 – 2018: Member of the Board of Directors of Bertelsmann SE &amp; Co. KGaA 2005 – 2018: Managing Director of RTL Television und Mediengruppe RTL Deutschland GmbH 2012 – 2017: Co-CEO of RTL Group S.A. (Luxembourg) 1995 – 2005: CFO (until 1998), since 1999 Managing Director of VOX Film- und Fernseh GmbH &amp; Co. KG 1991 – 1995: Various positions at RTL Television 1988 – 1991: Various positions at Bertelsmann AG 1982 – 1988: Studies in Business Administration at Universität Paderborn, degree: Diplom-Kauffrau (business graduate)  Status: 01/2026  Prof. Dr. Christoph M. Schmidt President of the Leibniz Association, University Professor Prof. Dr. Dr. h.c. Christoph M. Schmidt  President of the Leibniz Association, University Professor. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2021, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1962 Nationalities: German, Australian  Since 2026: President of the Leibniz Association (Wissenschaftsgemeinschaft Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz e.V.) Since 2002: Professor for economic policy and applied econometrics at Ruhr-Universität Bochum 2024 – 2026: Member of the Commission of Experts for Research and Innovation (EFI) 2020 – 2026: Vice president science of the German Academy of Science and Engineering (acatech) 2002 – 2026: President of RWI – Leibniz Institute for Economic Research e.V. Essen 2019 – 2022: Member of the Franco-German Council of Economic Experts (2020 – 2022: co-chair) 2009 – 2020: Member of the German Council of Economic Experts (2013 – 2020: chair) 1999 – 2002: Program Director „Evaluation of Labour Market Policies and Projects”, Institute of Labour Economics (IZA), Bonn 1995 – 2002: Professor for Econometrics at Alfred-Weber-Institut (AWI) at Ruprecht-Karls-Universität Heidelberg (ordinarius &amp; co-chair of AWI since 1996) 1991 – 1995: Research assistant and DFG (German Research Foundation) habilitation scholar at Seminar for Labour and Population Economics (SELAPO), Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München 1991 – 1995: Habilitation at Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München 1987 – 1991: Ph.D. in Economics at Princeton University (USA) 1981 – 1987: Studies in Economics at Universität Mannheim, degree: Diplom-Volkswirt (graduate economist)  Status: 07/2026  Dr. Vishal Sikka Founder and CEO of Vianai Systems, Inc. Dr. Vishal Sikka  Founder and CEO of Vianai Systems, Inc. (not publicly listed) Shareholder representative</data>
