      <data key="e_source_url">https://www.credit-agricole.com/en/group/governance</data>
      <data key="e_quote">Crédit Agricole S.A. so leans on the values of transparency, responsibility and efficiency, what is translated in the organization and the functioning of the Board of Directors by:  • The very active implication of the directors in the corporate life of the company, as well as in the control of its management and its strategy;  • The will to search for the opening and for the balance in the organization of the powers and the composition of governing bodies;  • The permanent concern to allow each to exercise effectively the responsibilities with the necessary objectivity and the independence, in particular through the quality of the dialogue and the transparency of the information.  Click here to find out more on governance Board of directors - as of 16 June 2026 Specialised committees of board Executive committee - as of November 1st, 2026 Management committee - as of November 1st, 2026 DIRECTORS ELECTED BY THE ANNUAL GENERAL MEETING Eric VIAL Chairman of the Board of Directors Chairman of the Social Engagement Committee Member of the Strategy and Technology Committee and of the Appointments and Governance Committee Raphaël APPERT SAS Rue La Boétie represented by Raphaël Appert Deputy Chairman of the Board of Directors Member of the Strategy and Technology Committee, Societal Commitment Committee and of the Appointments and Governance Committee Franck ALEXANDRE Director</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="e712" source="franck-saudo" target="safran">
      <data key="e_predicate">board_member</data>
      <data key="e_edge_class">network</data>
      <data key="e_role">employed_by</data>
      <data key="e_grade">A</data>
      <data key="e_n_sources">1</data>
      <data key="e_doc_id">official-safran-governance</data>
      <data key="e_doc_title">official-safran-governance</data>
      <data key="e_doc_path">sources/official/safran-governance.txt</data>
      <data key="e_source_url">https://www.safran-group.com/group/profile/governance</data>
      <data key="e_quote">Safran  We value your privacy  We use cookies to enhance your browsing experience, serve personalised ads or content, and analyse our traffic. By clicking "Accept All", you consent to our use of cookies.  Customise Reject All Accept All Necessary Functional Analytics Performance Advertisement Save My Preferences Skip to main content SAF 287.2€ +4.17% Countries Locations Companies Graphic guidelines EN Logins Open search GROUP SUSTAINABILITY PRODUCTS &amp; SERVICES CAREERS FINANCE NEWS &amp; MEDIA Home Group Profile Governance Governance  Safran is a French-registered company, listed on NYSE Euronext Paris. Its share is part of the CAC 40 French stock market index, and of the European market index, Euro Stoxx 50. An Executive Committee representing the Group's different businesses implements the strategic objectives defined by the Board of Directors. This governance principle guarantees a balance of power, and ensures Safran’s agility to meet the changing requirements of its economic, financial and competitive environment.  Ross McInnes, Chairman of the Board of Safran, and Olivier Andriès, Chief Executive Officer of Safran Board of Directors  Ross McInnes  Group Chairman of the Board  SEE PROFILE  Olivier Andriès  Safran Chief Executive Officer and Director  SEE PROFILE  Anne Aubert  Group Director representing employee shareholders  SEE PROFILE  Valérie Baudson  Group Independent Director, Member and Chair of the Appointments and Compensation Committee  SEE PROFILE  Fabrice Brégier  Group Independent Director, Member of the Innovation, Technology &amp; Climate Committee  SEE PROFILE  Anne Bouverot  Group Independant Director, Member of the Innovation, Technology &amp; Climate Committee  SEE PROFILE  Christèle Debarenne-Fievet  Group Director representing employees, Member of the Appointments and Compensation Committee  SEE PROFILE  Pascale Dosda  Group Director representing employee shareholders  SEE PROFILE  Laurent Guillot  Group Independant Director, Member and Chair of the Audit and Risk Committee, Member of the Innovation, Technology &amp; Climate Committee  SEE PROFILE  Ivan Hardouin  Group Director representing employees, Member of the Audit and Risk Committee, Member of the Innovation, Technology &amp; Climate Committee  SEE PROFILE  Guillemette Kreis  French State Representative, Member of the Audit and Risk Committee, Member of the Appointments and Compensation Committee  SEE PROFILE  Alexandre Lahousse  Group Director proposed by the French State, Member of the Innovation, Technology &amp; Climate Committee  SEE PROFILE  Fabienne Lecorvaisier  Group Independent Director, Member of the Audit and Risk Committee, Member of the Innovation, Technology &amp; Climate Committee, Member of the Appointments and Compensation Committee  SEE PROFILE  Patrick Pélata  Group Lead Independent Director, Director responsible for monitoring climate issues, Member and Chair of the Innovation, Technology &amp; Climate Committee, Member of the Appointments and Compensation Committee, member of the Audit and Risk Committee  SEE PROFILE  Robert Peugeot  Group Independent Director, Member of the Audit and Risk Committee  SEE PROFILE  Daniela Schwarzer  Independent Director  SEE PROFILE SAFRAN - ARTICLES OF INCORPORATION AND BYLAWS BOARD OF DIRECTORS - INTERNAL RULES SAFRAN’S BOARD OF DIRECTORS – KEY FIGURES 2 EMPLOYEE REPRESENTATIVES 2 EMPLOYEE SHAREHOLDER REPRESENTATIVES 8 INDEPENDENT DIRECTORS An independent, representative board  The composition of the Board of Directors ensures that it can make objective, enlightened decisions. The 16 members of the Board include 8 independent directors (equal to 66.7% of the Board, according to the calculation criteria in the AFEP-MEDEF code*), offering a wide range of complementary expertise. One State representative and one director are proposed by the State. The Board of Directors also includes two employee shareholder representatives and two employee representatives, meaning that all stakeholders involved in Safran's daily affairs are represented. There are 8 women (equal to 50% of the Board, employee shareholder and employee representatives excluded), and 10 directors with international profiles. The Board features permanent "guests" with a consultative voice: a government commissioner and the Group’s Social and Economic Committee representative.  *Directors representing employee shareholders and Directors representing employees are not taken into account in these calculations  Permanent board committees  Each of the Board committees, acting within its scope of expertise, provides in-depth analysis prior to the Board's deliberations to support its decisions. They issue proposals, opinions and recommendations to the Board.  Audit and Risk Committee: this committee exercises meticulous control over Safran's financial statements and information. It also oversees the efficiency of the Group's internal control and risk management systems.  Members: Laurent Guillot (Chairman) Ivan Hardouin Guillemette Kreis Fabienne Lecorvaisier Robert Peugeot Patrick Pélata  Appointments and Compensation Committee: with a majority of independent directors, this committee assists the Board in selecting its members and corporate officers. It also draws up recommendations and proposals concerning the compensation of corporate officers.  Members: Valérie Baudson (Chair) Christèle Debarenne-Fievet Guillemette Kreis Fabienne Lecorvaisier Patrick Pelata  Innovation, Technology &amp; Climate Committee: missions of this Committee are to examine the strategic orientations and options taken by the Group regarding innovation, research and technology, developments of new products and services, to follow-up on associated global road maps and technological trends and evolutions, as well as to examine the Executive Management's climate action plan.  Members: Patrick Pelata (Chairman) Anne Bouverot Fabrice Brégier Laurent Guillot Ivan Hardouin Alexandre Lahousse Fabienne Lecorvaisier  Executive Committee  Olivier Andriès  Safran Chief Executive Officer and Director  SEE PROFILE  Eric Dalbiès  EVP, Chief Technology Officer  SEE PROFILE  Pascal Bantegnie  Chief Financial Officer  SEE PROFILE  Stéphane Dubois  EVP, Corporate Human and Social Responsibility  SEE PROFILE  Philippe Errera  EVP, International Development and Government Relations  SEE PROFILE  Marjolaine Grange  EVP, Industrial, Purchasing and Performance  SEE PROFILE  Kate Philipps  EVP, Group Communications  SEE PROFILE  Karine Stamens  EVP, Corporate Secretary, Chairman of the Compliance, Ethics and Anti-fraud Committee  SEE PROFILE  Nathalie Stubler  Chief Sustainability Officer  SEE PROFILE  Frédéric Verger  EVP, Chief Digital Officer and Chief Information Officer  SEE PROFILE  François Bastin  CEO, Safran Landing Systems  SEE PROFILE  Bruno Bellanger  CEO, Safran Electrical &amp; Power  SEE PROFILE  Vincent Caro  CEO, Safran Nacelles  SEE PROFILE  Stéphane Cueille  CEO, Safran Aircraft Engines  SEE PROFILE  Cédric Goubet  CEO, Safran Helicopter Engines  SEE PROFILE  Victoria Foy  CEO, Safran Seats  SEE PROFILE  Franck Saudo  CEO, Safran Electronics &amp; Defense</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="e713" source="franco-ceruti" target="intesa-sanpaolo">
      <data key="e_predicate">board_member</data>
      <data key="e_edge_class">network</data>
