e BMW AG Works Council Dingolfing Since 1995: Member of the BMW AG Works Council Dingolfing (full-time Member since 1998) 1985 – 1998: Electronics technician in car body manufacturing 1985: Joined BMW AG Apprenticeship power plant electronics technician and metal-working foreman  Status: 01/2026  Dr. Kurt Bock Chairman of the Supervisory Board of BASF SE Dr. Kurt Bock  Deputy Chairman of the Supervisory Board. Chairman of the Supervisory Board of BASF SE. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2018, Deputy Chairman since 2021, Chairman of the Audit Committee since 2020, elected until 2027 Year of birth: 1958 Nationality: German  Since 2020: Chairman of the Supervisory Board of BASF SE 2011 – 2018: Chairman of the Board of Executive Directors of BASF SE 2003 – 2011: Member of the Board of Executive Directors and CFO of BASF AG (BASF SE since 2008), since 2007 also Chairman and CEO of BASF Corporation (USA) 2000 – 2002: President of Logistics and Information Services, BASF AG 1998 – 2000: CFO of BASF Corporation (USA) 1996 – 1998: Managing Director, Robert Bosch Ltda. (Brazil) 1992 – 1996: Senior Vice President Finance and Accounting, Robert Bosch GmbH 1991 – 1992: Head of Technology, Director Planning and Controlling for Engineering Plastics, BASF AG 1985 – 1991: Various functions in the finance division of BASF AG 1985: Ph.D. (Dr. rer. pol.) at Universität Bonn 1977 – 1985: Studies in Business Administration at Westfälische Wilhelms-Universität Münster and Universität zu Köln as well as at Pennsylvania State University (USA)  Status: 01/2026  Ulrich Bauer Member of the Works Council Munich Ulrich Bauer  Member of the BMW AG Works Council Munich. Employee representative.  Mandate: Member since 2024, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1964 Nationality: German  Since 2014: Full-time Member of the BMW AG Works Council Munich 2012 – 2014: Head of Marketing, BMW Financial Services 2010 – 2012: Head of Marketing and Sales Services, BMW Bank GmbH 2001 – 2010: Head of Sales Management, BMW Bank GmbH; from 2007 also head of Business Line Retail 1998 – 2001: Head of European Sales Processes and Direct Banking, BMW Bank GmbH 1994 – 1998: Project manager at Roland Berger &amp; Partner 1992 – 1994: Trainee and Head of Operations Organization at Allianz Property Insurance, Stuttgart branch 1985 – 1990: Working student and freelancer at IBM Deutschland GmbH 1986 – 1991: Studies in Economics at Universität Hohenheim, degree: Dipl.-Oec. (graduate economist)  Status: 01/2026  Dr. Marc Bitzer Chairman and CEO of Whirlpool Corp. Dr. Marc Bitzer  Chairman and CEO of Whirlpool Corp. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2021, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1965 Nationality: German, US-American  Since 2017: Chairman and CEO of Whirlpool Corp. (USA) Since 1990: Co-Founder and Member of the Board of Directors of Simex Trading AG (Switzerland) 1999 – 2017: Various management positions at Whirlpool Corp. in Italy and North America 1991 – 1999: The Boston Consulting Group with assignments in Munich and Toronto (Canada), most recently as Vice President, Recruiting Director and member of the German Consumer Goods Practice Group 1984 – 1991: Studies in Economics and Ph.D. (Dr. oec.) at Universität St. Gallen (Switzerland)  Status: 01/2026  Dr. Christian Bruch CEO of Siemens Energy AG. Dr.-Ing. Christian Bruch  CEO of Siemens Energy AG. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2026, elected until 2030 Year of birth: 1970 Nationality: German  Since 2020: CEO, Siemens Energy AG Since 2020: CEO, Siemens Energy Management GmbH 2019 – 2020: Spokesperson of the Board of Management, Linde AG 2019 – 2020: Executive Vice President and CEO Linde Engineering, Linde plc (Ireland) 2015 – 2018: Member of the Board of Management, Linde AG (Engineering Division, corporate and support function Technology &amp; Innovation, Digitalisation) 2004 – 2015: Various management positions, Linde AG (Gases Division and Engineering Division) 2000 – 2004: Projekt engineer, RWE AG; from 2002 on: Head of Research and Project Development at RWE Fuel Cells GmbH 1997 – 2000: Research engineer at ETH Zurich (Switzerland); Ph.D. in engineering (Dr.-Ing.) 1991 – 1997: Studies in mechanical engineering at Leibniz Universität Hannover and the University of Strathclyde Glasgow (UK); degree: graduate engineer  Status: 05/2026  Rachel Empey Member of supervisory boards Rachel Empey  Member of supervisory boards. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2021, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1976 Nationalities: British, German  Since 2025: Member of the Supervisory Board and the Audit Committee of Deutsche Telekom AG (since 2026: Chairwoman of the Audit Committee) Since 2024: Member of the Foundation Board of Else Kröner-Fresenius-Stiftung Since 2023: Member of the Supervisory Board and the Audit Committee of ZF Friedrichshafen AG 2017 – 2022: CFO of Fresenius Management SE 2016 – 2021: Non-Executive Director and member of the Audit Committee of Inchcape plc (UK) 2011 – 2017: Member of the Management Board of Telefónica Deutschland Holding AG (Finance, Strategy and Innovation); Joint Leader of the Board, General Manager of Operating Business (2014) 2003 – 2011: Various positions in the Telefónica Group in the UK and Germany 2002 – 2003: Commercial Director, Weir Group plc (UK) 2000 – 2002: Business Analyst, Lucent Technologies (UK) 2000: Studies at the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales (ICAEW), degree: Chartered Accountant 1997 – 2000: Audit Executive at Ernst &amp; Young Ltd., Bristol (UK) 1994 ­­– 1997: Studies in Mathematics at the University of Oxford (UK)  Status: 04/2026  Dr. h.c. Susanne Klatten Entrepreneur Dr. h.c. Susanne Klatten  Entrepreneur. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 1997, elected until 2028 Year of birth: 1962 Nationality: German  Since 1991: Independent entrepreneur 1988: Studies at the International Institute for Management Development (Lausanne, Switzer