pate its refinancing needs. The bonds  were oversubscribed almost three times over, reflecting  investors’ confidence in the Group’s credit quality. April Saint-Gobain included in the CDP’s “List A”  For the second year in a row, Saint-Gobain is on the  CDP’s prestigious “Climate List,” which rewards its  leadership in environmental transparency and climate  action. Only 2% of the companies assessed receive this  distinction, highlighting the Group’s strong sustainability  strategy. Sustainable construction: global trends revealed by the third edition of the Saint-Gobain barometer  The third edition of the Sustainable Construction  Barometer reveals a growing global awareness and  urgency concerning sustainable construction practices.  Based on surveys conducted in 27 countries, the study  highlights the main regional differences and the need to  strengthen training and actions to accelerate the sector’s  transformation. May Saint-Gobain to launch its first low-carbon stone  wool insulation plant in the United Kingdom Saint-Gobain will build a new low-carbon stone wool  insulation plant in Melton Mowbray. Equipped with a fully  electric furnace powered by renewable energy, the plant  will produce 50,000 tonnes per year, meeting the United  Kingdom's growing demand for sustainable building  materials. June Saint-Gobain launches its world’s lowest-carbon  insulation plant in Finland  Saint-Gobain has unveiled the production of very low- carbon glass wool at its Forssa site in Finland. Fully  powered by biogas and hydropower, the plant will  reduce CO₂ emissions by 1,500 tonnes per year and  reduce the carbon footprint of its products by up to 40%. PRESENTING SAINT-GOBAIN SAINT-GOBAIN TODAY 36 SAINT-GOBAIN • UNIVERSAL REGISTRATION DOCUMENT 2025 Ë www.saint-gobain.com General Shareholders’ Meeting and Board of Directors  Meeting on June 5, 2025  Saint-Gobain shareholders reappointed Benoit Bazin as  Chief Executive Officer and approved a 5% dividend  increase, to €2.20 