d of Sales Management, BMW Bank GmbH; from 2007 also head of Business Line Retail 1998 – 2001: Head of European Sales Processes and Direct Banking, BMW Bank GmbH 1994 – 1998: Project manager at Roland Berger &amp; Partner 1992 – 1994: Trainee and Head of Operations Organization at Allianz Property Insurance, Stuttgart branch 1985 – 1990: Working student and freelancer at IBM Deutschland GmbH 1986 – 1991: Studies in Economics at Universität Hohenheim, degree: Dipl.-Oec. (graduate economist)  Status: 01/2026  Dr. Marc Bitzer Chairman and CEO of Whirlpool Corp. Dr. Marc Bitzer  Chairman and CEO of Whirlpool Corp. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2021, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1965 Nationality: German, US-American  Since 2017: Chairman and CEO of Whirlpool Corp. (USA) Since 1990: Co-Founder and Member of the Board of Directors of Simex Trading AG (Switzerland) 1999 – 2017: Various management positions at Whirlpool Corp. in Italy and North America 1991 – 1999: The Boston Consulting Group with assignments in Munich and Toronto (Canada), most recently as Vice President, Recruiting Director and member of the German Consumer Goods Practice Group 1984 – 1991: Studies in Economics and Ph.D. (Dr. oec.) at Universität St. Gallen (Switzerland)  Status: 01/2026  Dr. Christian Bruch CEO of Siemens Energy AG. Dr.-Ing. Christian Bruch  CEO of Siemens Energy AG. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2026, elected until 2030 Year of birth: 1970 Nationality: German  Since 2020: CEO, Siemens Energy AG Since 2020: CEO, Siemens Energy Management GmbH 2019 – 2020: Spokesperson of the Board of Management, Linde AG 2019 – 2020: Executive Vice President and CEO Linde Engineering, Linde plc (Ireland) 2015 – 2018: Member of the Board of Management, Linde AG (Engineering Division, corporate and support function Technology &amp; Innovation, Digitalisation) 2004 – 2015: Various management positions, Linde AG (Gases Division and Engineering Division) 2000 – 2004: Projekt engineer, RWE AG; from 2002 on: Head of Research and Project Development at RWE Fuel Cells GmbH 1997 – 2000: Research engineer at ETH Zurich (Switzerland); Ph.D. in engineering (Dr.-Ing.) 1991 – 1997: Studies in mechanical engineering at Leibniz Universität Hannover and the University of Strathclyde Glasgow (UK); degree: graduate engineer  Status: 05/2026  Rachel Empey Member of supervisory boards Rachel Empey  Member of supervisory boards. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 2021, elected until 2029 Year of birth: 1976 Nationalities: British, German  Since 2025: Member of the Supervisory Board and the Audit Committee of Deutsche Telekom AG (since 2026: Chairwoman of the Audit Committee) Since 2024: Member of the Foundation Board of Else Kröner-Fresenius-Stiftung Since 2023: Member of the Supervisory Board and the Audit Committee of ZF Friedrichshafen AG 2017 – 2022: CFO of Fresenius Management SE 2016 – 2021: Non-Executive Director and member of the Audit Committee of Inchcape plc (UK) 2011 – 2017: Member of the Management Board of Telefónica Deutschland Holding AG (Finance, Strategy and Innovation); Joint Leader of the Board, General Manager of Operating Business (2014) 2003 – 2011: Various positions in the Telefónica Group in the UK and Germany 2002 – 2003: Commercial Director, Weir Group plc (UK) 2000 – 2002: Business Analyst, Lucent Technologies (UK) 2000: Studies at the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales (ICAEW), degree: Chartered Accountant 1997 – 2000: Audit Executive at Ernst &amp; Young Ltd., Bristol (UK) 1994 ­­– 1997: Studies in Mathematics at the University of Oxford (UK)  Status: 04/2026  Dr. h.c. Susanne Klatten Entrepreneur Dr. h.c. Susanne Klatten  Entrepreneur. Shareholder representative.  Mandate: Member since 1997, elected until 2028 Year of birth: 1962 Nationality: German  Since 1991: Independent entrepreneur 1988: Studies at the International Institute for Management Development (Lausanne, Switzer