      <data key="e_doc_id">official-sap-supervisory-board</data>
      <data key="e_doc_title">official-sap-supervisory-board</data>
      <data key="e_doc_path">sources/official/sap-supervisory-board.txt</data>
      <data key="e_source_url">https://www.sap.com/investors/en/governance-and-sustainability/supervisory-board.html</data>
      <data key="e_quote">SAP Investor Relations Ihre Einstellungen zu Cookies für diese Website  Diese Website verwendet Cookies und verwandte Technologien entsprechend der Beschreibung in unserer Cookie-Erklärung, u. A. zum fehlerfreien Betrieb, zur Analyse, für eine verbesserte Benutzerfreundlichkeit oder zu Werbezwecken. Sie können unserer Verwendung dieser Technologien zustimmen oder Ihre eigenen Präferenzen verwalten.  Datenschutzerklärung | Cookie-Erklärung  Alle annehmen Alle ablehnen Einstellungen verwalten Skip to Content Financial Documents &amp; EventsStockNewsGovernance &amp; SustainabilityInvestor ResourcesExplore SAP Contact Us / Governance &amp; Sustainability Supervisory Board Members Committees Profile of Skills and Expertise Qualification Matrix Meeting Participation SAP SE Corporate Governance  SAP SE Supervisory Board  The SAP SE Supervisory Board advises and supervises the Executive Board. The number of members in and the composition of the Supervisory Board are determined by the Articles of Incorporation and the Agreement of the Involvement of the European Employees in SAP SE. SAP's Supervisory Board currently comprises nine members elected by the shareholders at their General Meeting and nine members representing the European employees of the SAP group.  Dr. h. c. mult. Pekka Ala-Pietilae  Chairman of the Supervisory Board SAP SE Chairperson of the Board of Directors of HERE Technologies B.V., Amsterdam, Netherlands  Year of Birth: 1957  Nationality: Finnish  First elected: 2024  Term expires: 2027  Learn more about Dr. h. c. mult. Pekka Ala-Pietilae  Lars Lamadé  Deputy Chairperson of the Supervisory Board of SAP SE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="e982" source="laura-barlow" target="societe-generale">
      <data key="e_predicate">board_member</data>
      <data key="e_edge_class">network</data>
      <data key="e_role">board_member</data>
      <data key="e_grade">A</data>
      <data key="e_n_sources">1</data>
      <data key="e_doc_id">official-societe-generale-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_doc_title">official-societe-generale-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_doc_path">sources/official/societe-generale-board-of-directors.txt</data>
      <data key="e_source_url">https://www.societegenerale.com/en/group/governance/board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_quote">Société Générale official governance page Welcome to the Societe Generale group website.  Societe Generale and its partners use cookies or equivalent technologies to ensure the proper functioning and security of the site, to improve your experience, to personalise and improve the performance of advertisements and content, to compile traffic and browsing statistics, and to enable you to share content on social networks.  Some of these cookies are subject to your consent. You can express your choice globally, or set your preferences by cookie purpose. You can change these choices at any time.  View our partners Set up Decline all Accept all Go to main content Facebook Twitter Linkedin Instagram YouTube Homepage Locations 60.84€ (-0.25%) FR | EN The Group Responsibility News and documentation Investors Job applicants Search breadcrumb You are here: Home The Group Governance Board of Directors Governance The Board of Directors  The Board of Directors represents all shareholders. It has fifteen members: thirteen Directors appointed by the Shareholders’ Annual General Meeting, including one representing employee shareholders, and two representing employees in general, directly elected by their peers. A non-voting Director has also been appointed to assist the Board with all matters relating to social and environmental responsibility.  The Board of Directors  The Board of Directors collectively represents all shareholders. It acts in the social interest of the Bank and ensures its proper function. Its missions are to approve strategic guidelines, monitor and ensure their implementation in line with Societe Generale's values, and comply with the highest international standards of governance, ethics and risk management. Its members are chosen for their experience, expertise and independence. The Board of Directors aims to be composed of an equal number of men and women and to reflect diversity.  Filter by name William Connelly Chairman of the Board of Directors Independent Director Company Director See more William Connelly informations Slawomir Krupa  Chief Executive Officer  See more Slawomir Krupa informations Ingrid-Helen Arnold Chief Executive Officer of KAKO GmbH (Germany) Independent Director Company Director Member of the Risk Committee See more Ingrid-Helen Arnold informations Laura Barlow Independent Director</data>
    </edge>
