es and support the Group to ensure it acts     The Compensation Committee reviews the Company’s              in accordance with external regulations and internal policies. compensation system and principles. The Head of Human             It supports Nestlé’s management to raise risk awareness Resources may attend the meetings, except when questions          and to anticipate emerging risks, as well as the process of compensation for Executive Board members are                   of identifying appropriate mitigation actions. deliberated.                                                          The Nestlé Group adopts a dual approach using “Top-     Additional information and control instruments include        Down” and “Bottom-Up” assessments. The “Top-Down” the external auditors, Ernst &amp; Young Ltd, auditors of             assessment occurs annually and focuses on the Group’s Nestlé S.A. and of the Consolidated Financial Statements          global risks. A “Bottom‑Up” assessment occurs in parallel, of the Nestlé Group, who conduct their audit in compliance        resulting in the aggregation of individual assessments by with Swiss law and in accordance with Swiss Auditing              all Markets, Regionally and Globally Managed Businesses. Standards and International Standards on Auditing, and the            Additionally, Nestlé engages with external stakeholders Nestlé Internal Audit function.                                   to better understand the issues that are of most concern to     Nestlé Internal Audit comprises an organization of one        them. For each issue, the materiality matrix (please refer to Center Team and eight regional units of auditors covering         the Non-Financial Statement) rates the degree of stakeholder all the businesses (i.e. head offices, factories, distribution    concern and potential business impact. centers and business units) worldwide, completing audit               Group ERM combines the output of the “Top-Down” assign