      <data key="e_doc_title">official-credit-agricole-governance</data>
      <data key="e_doc_path">sources/official/credit-agricole-governance.txt</data>
      <data key="e_source_url">https://www.credit-agricole.com/en/group/governance</data>
      <data key="e_quote">Crédit Agricole S.A. so leans on the values of transparency, responsibility and efficiency, what is translated in the organization and the functioning of the Board of Directors by:  • The very active implication of the directors in the corporate life of the company, as well as in the control of its management and its strategy;  • The will to search for the opening and for the balance in the organization of the powers and the composition of governing bodies;  • The permanent concern to allow each to exercise effectively the responsibilities with the necessary objectivity and the independence, in particular through the quality of the dialogue and the transparency of the information.  Click here to find out more on governance Board of directors - as of 16 June 2026 Specialised committees of board Executive committee - as of November 1st, 2026 Management committee - as of November 1st, 2026 DIRECTORS ELECTED BY THE ANNUAL GENERAL MEETING Eric VIAL Chairman of the Board of Directors Chairman of the Social Engagement Committee Member of the Strategy and Technology Committee and of the Appointments and Governance Committee Raphaël APPERT SAS Rue La Boétie represented by Raphaël Appert Deputy Chairman of the Board of Directors Member of the Strategy and Technology Committee, Societal Commitment Committee and of the Appointments and Governance Committee Franck ALEXANDRE Director Membre of the Societal Commitment Committee Agnès AUDIER Independent Director Chairwoman of the Compensation Committee Member of the Audit Commitee and of the Strategy and Technology Committee Olivier AUFFRAY Director Member of the Strategy and Technology Committee, the Compensation Committee, and the Nomination and Governance Committee Sonia BONNET-BERNARD Independent Director Chairwoman of the Audit Committee Member of the Risks Committee Pierre CAMBEFORT Director</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="e1287" source="pierre-chaussoneaux" target="orange">
      <data key="e_predicate">board_member</data>
      <data key="e_edge_class">network</data>
      <data key="e_role">board_member</data>
      <data key="e_grade">A</data>
      <data key="e_n_sources">1</data>
      <data key="e_doc_id">official-orange-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_doc_title">official-orange-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_doc_path">sources/official/orange-board-of-directors.txt</data>
      <data key="e_source_url">https://www.orange.com/en/our-group/our-governance/our-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_quote">Orange and their partners use cookies (or equivalent technologies).  With your agreement, we and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on the link in the footer or in our Cookie policy on this website.  We and our partners process data for the following purposes: Analytics, Digital Accessibility, Personalised advertising and content, advertising and content measurement, audience research and services development, Precise geolocation data, and identification through device scanning, Store and/or access information on a device, Technical Cookies, User Feedback  View our 12 partners Customize Disagree Agree Skip to main content Orange Business All our sites Media library  ORA  14,45€  -0,14%  Confort+ FR EN Our Group Our impact Our expertise Our news Finance Press Careers Search on the website Homepage Our governance Our Board of directors Our Board of directors Our Board of Directors, shaping Orange’s future  The Board oversees all decisions tied to Orange’s major strategic, economic, social, financial, technological and environmental priorities. Medium-term direction for the Group is set through a strategic plan that is updated regularly. The CEO presents this plan to the Board, which then reviews and adopts it. The plan includes projected trends for key operational, social and financial indicators to ensure alignment with market developments.  The balance and stability of the Council  Bloc Exergue Item 15 members  make up Orange's Board of Directors.  Bloc Exergue Item 7 independent directors  ensuring a balance of power  Bloc Exergue Item 4 years  the term of office of each director  A balanced Board for effective governance  Orange’s Board of Directors brings together 15 members with varied backgrounds: seven independent directors, three representing the public sector, three representing employees and one representing employee shareholders (currently vacant). This diversity of experience and expertise ensures balance, independence and strong oversight. Each director serves a four-year term, in line with the bylaws updated at the Annual Shareholders’ Meeting on May 19, 2022.  Our commitment to the highest standards in governance  In corporate governance, Orange follows the recommendations of the Afep-Medef Code (“Corporate Governance Code for Listed Companies”) as revised in December 2022. This document can be viewed in the “Governance Documentation” section of our site and is also available on the Afep and Medef websites.  Orange’s Board ensures that the key pillars of our Trust the Future strategic plan are carried out effectively. It reviews the major milestones of the Group’s activity, including operational performance, quarterly results, half-year and annual accounts, budget, risk factors and sustainability status. It also determines the compensation of company directors and examines major strategic projects, including significant portfolio operations and long-term investments.  Board composition  Frédéric Sanchez Chairman of the Board, Independent Director  Christel Heydemann Chief Executive Officer, Director  Nicolas Guérin Secretary General  Independent Directors  Jacques Aschenbroich Valérie Beaulieu Alexandre Bompard Anne-Gabrielle Heilbronner Gilles Grapinet Momar Nguer Frédéric Sanchez  Directors representing the public sector  Guillemette Kreis Anne Lange Thierry Sommelet (Bpifrance Participations)  Director representing employees  Nadia Zak Calvet  Directors elected by the employees  Pierre Chaussoneaux</data>
    </edge>
