    <edge id="e1512" source="vincent-gimeno" target="orange">
      <data key="e_predicate">board_member</data>
      <data key="e_edge_class">network</data>
      <data key="e_role">board_member</data>
      <data key="e_grade">A</data>
      <data key="e_n_sources">1</data>
      <data key="e_doc_id">official-orange-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_doc_title">official-orange-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_doc_path">sources/official/orange-board-of-directors.txt</data>
      <data key="e_source_url">https://www.orange.com/en/our-group/our-governance/our-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_quote">Orange and their partners use cookies (or equivalent technologies).  With your agreement, we and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on the link in the footer or in our Cookie policy on this website.  We and our partners process data for the following purposes: Analytics, Digital Accessibility, Personalised advertising and content, advertising and content measurement, audience research and services development, Precise geolocation data, and identification through device scanning, Store and/or access information on a device, Technical Cookies, User Feedback  View our 12 partners Customize Disagree Agree Skip to main content Orange Business All our sites Media library  ORA  14,45€  -0,14%  Confort+ FR EN Our Group Our impact Our expertise Our news Finance Press Careers Search on the website Homepage Our governance Our Board of directors Our Board of directors Our Board of Directors, shaping Orange’s future  The Board oversees all decisions tied to Orange’s major strategic, economic, social, financial, technological and environmental priorities. Medium-term direction for the Group is set through a strategic plan that is updated regularly. The CEO presents this plan to the Board, which then reviews and adopts it. The plan includes projected trends for key operational, social and financial indicators to ensure alignment with market developments.  The balance and stability of the Council  Bloc Exergue Item 15 members  make up Orange's Board of Directors.  Bloc Exergue Item 7 independent directors  ensuring a balance of power  Bloc Exergue Item 4 years  the term of office of each director  A balanced Board for effective governance  Orange’s Board of Directors brings together 15 members with varied backgrounds: seven independent directors, three representing the public sector, three representing employees and one representing employee shareholders (currently vacant). This diversity of experience and expertise ensures balance, independence and strong oversight. Each director serves a four-year term, in line with the bylaws updated at the Annual Shareholders’ Meeting on May 19, 2022.  Our commitment to the highest standards in governance  In corporate governance, Orange follows the recommendations of the Afep-Medef Code (“Corporate Governance Code for Listed Companies”) as revised in December 2022. This document can be viewed in the “Governance Documentation” section of our site and is also available on the Afep and Medef websites.  Orange’s Board ensures that the key pillars of our Trust the Future strategic plan are carried out effectively. It reviews the major milestones of the Group’s activity, including operational performance, quarterly results, half-year and annual accounts, budget, risk factors and sustainability status. It also determines the compensation of company directors and examines major strategic projects, including significant portfolio operations and long-term investments.  Board composition  Frédéric Sanchez Chairman of the Board, Independent Director  Christel Heydemann Chief Executive Officer, Director  Nicolas Guérin Secretary General  Independent Directors  Jacques Aschenbroich Valérie Beaulieu Alexandre Bompard Anne-Gabrielle Heilbronner Gilles Grapinet Momar Nguer Frédéric Sanchez  Directors representing the public sector  Guillemette Kreis Anne Lange Thierry Sommelet (Bpifrance Participations)  Director representing employees  Nadia Zak Calvet  Directors elected by the employees  Pierre Chaussoneaux Vincent Gimeno</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="e1513" source="vincenzo-cariello" target="unicredit">
      <data key="e_predicate">board_member</data>
      <data key="e_edge_class">network</data>
      <data key="e_role">board_member</data>
      <data key="e_grade">A</data>
      <data key="e_n_sources">1</data>
      <data key="e_doc_id">official-unicredit-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_doc_title">official-unicredit-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_doc_path">sources/official/unicredit-board-of-directors.txt</data>
      <data key="e_source_url">https://www.unicreditgroup.eu/en/governance/governance-bodies/board-of-directors.html</data>
      <data key="e_quote">UniCredit  Consent to the use of cookies  This website uses technical, analytics and profiling Cookies, also installed by third parties (so called Third-Party Cookies).  Profiling Cookies are used in order to offer you advertising messages in line with your preferences ; their installation requires your prior consent .  Further information on the cookies installed through this website are available by accessing the Cookie Policy , always available on this website.  By clicking on the X at the top right, your navigation will continue without profiling cookies.  ACCEPT ALL COOKIES  MORE INFO  Messaggio  Skip to:  Secondary Menu Content Footer  Close Hamburger  MAGAZINE  FAQ  CALENDAR  WORLDWIDE  EN  Language  ITALIANO  ENGLISH  DEUTSCH --&gt;  BACK  Strategy  About us  Governance  Investors  Press &amp; Media  Careers  Strategy  With UniCredit Unlimited, we are stepping into a new era. One defined by bold ambition and a fundamental shift in how a European bank operates.  Overview Page Strategy  Our Purpose  Our Business  Our Business  Overview Page Our Business  Our approach to business  Client Solutions  Our Investment Insights  Corporate Clients  Retail, Private and Wealth Management  Digital &amp; Data  Longevity  Our Financial Ambition  Our Structural Advantages  About us  UniCredit is a leading pan-European bank providing best-in-class solutions and services across Italy, Germany, Austria and Central &amp; Eastern Europe. Our vision is to be the Bank for Europe's Future, driven by our purpose to Empower Communities to Progress.  Overview Page About us  Organisational structure  Organisational structure  Overview Page Organisational structure  Controlled companies  Our Culture &amp; Values  ESG and Sustainability  ESG and Sustainability  Overview Page ESG and Sustainability  Environmental  Social  Governance  Sustainability Reporting  ESG Day  Awards and Recognitions  Awards and Recognitions  Overview Page Awards and Recognitions  Group  Diversity, Equity and Inclusion  Diversity, Equity and Inclusion  Overview Page Diversity, Equity and Inclusion  DE&amp;I Framework: promoting diversity and inclusion  Gender equality and inclusion in the workplace  Inclusive culture and inclusion at work  Beyond March 8, together  Art, Music and Sport  Art, Music and Sport  Overview Page Art, Music and Sport  Art  Music  Sport  ESG Sustainability Policies and Ratings  Read More  Governance  UniCredit is committed to the highest standards of corporate governance, ensuring transparency and accountability for all stakeholders.  Overview Page Governance  Our Governance System  Our Governance System  Overview Page Our Governance System  Articles of Association and Code of Ethics  Related Parties and Associated Persons  Shareholders  Shareholders  Overview Page Shareholders  Shareholders structure  Archive  FAQ  Corporate bodies  Corporate bodies  Overview Page Corporate bodies  Board of Directors  Selection process and composition  Independence  Board Committees  Audit Committee  Activities &amp; meetings attendance  Our internal control systems  Management  Remuneration  Remuneration  Overview Page Remuneration  Governance &amp; Compliance  Incentive systems  Directors and Auditors compensation  Internal Dealings  Internal Dealings  Overview Page Internal Dealings  Transactions  Individual Holdings  Investors  Access UniCredit’s latest financial information, shared transparently and promptly with the investor community.  Overview Page Investors  Financial reporting  Financial reporting  Overview Page Financial reporting  Financial Reports  Financial highlights  Third pillar of Basel 2 and Basel 3  Conferences &amp; Other Presentations  Financial press releases  Financial calendar  Group Results  Equity investors  Equity investors  Overview Page Equity investors  Share price  Share information  Dividends  Shareholders structure  Equity analysts  Consensus  Debt investors  Debt investors  Overview Page Debt investors  Fixed income and ESG presentations  Funding programmes and prospectuses  Credit Ratings  Fixed income analysts  ESG investors  Retail investors  Contacts  Alerts  Press &amp; Media  This section provides access to UniCredit’s press releases, media resources and corporate materials, offering journalists and industry professionals up-to-date information on the Group.  Overview Page Press &amp; Media  Press Releases  News  Social Media  Podcasts  Podcasts  Overview Page Podcasts  Conversations Unlocked  Press Kit  Events Calendar  Contacts  Careers  Find the latest job opportunities at UniCredit and explore how you can build your career within a leading pan-European bank.  Overview Page Careers  Well-being  Learning &amp; Growth  Compensation &amp; Benefits  Online Banking --&gt; Online Banking  MAGAZINE  FAQ  CALENDAR  WORLDWIDE  SEARCH  EN  Language  ITALIANO  ENGLISH  DEUTSCH --&gt;  Hamburger Menu  Online Banking --&gt; Online Banking  Search  Search  Home  Governance  Corporate bodies  Board of Directors  Share  Print  Send  --&gt;  Share this event on:  X  LinkedIn  --&gt;  Recomend this page  Thank you, we sent your recommendation to the desired recipient.  Sorry, this functionality is not available right now. Please try with this link . Thank you.  Sender:  Recipient (e-mail address):  Send  Back to Corporate Bodies  Board of Directors  Our Board of Directors can be made from a minimum of 9 up to a maximum of 19 members, of whom at least 3 - and, in any case, no more than 5 - make up the Audit Committee.  Directors' term in office is three financial years, unless a shorter term is established at the time of their appointment, and ends on the date of the Shareholders' Meeting called for the approval of the financial statements relating to the last financial year in which they are in office.  The Board of Directors currently in office was appointed by the ordinary Shareholders' Meeting on April 12, 2024 for the financial years 2024 - 2026, on the basis of a proportional representation mechanism ("voto di lista"), and its terms of office ends on the date of the Shareholders' Meeting called to approve the 2026 financial statements.  As regards the actions taken in recent years to strengthen our governance and align it with international best practices, improving the composition and functioning of the Board of Directors has been a fundamental commitment for our Group.  Board of Directors evolution  2017  2018  2019  2020  2021  2023  2024  Faculty to file its own list of candidates in the event of its renewal  Increase from 1 to 2 in the number of Directors appointed from the minority slates  Size of the Board of Directors reduced from 17 to 15, number of Vice Chairmen reduced from 3 to 1  Board's tenure equal to maximum 3 mandates  Increased diversity  Identified Digital &amp; Technology and Banking Business as the major competence areas to be developed within the Board  Size of the Board of Directors reduced from 15 to 14  Strengthen the Board of Directors' collective suitability through (i) broad coverage of financial services; (ii) exposure to international markets &amp; geographies; (iii) broad range of industrial &amp; digital expertise; (iv) increased diversity  Size of the Board of Directors reduced from 14 to 13  Size of the Board of Directors reduced from 13 to 12  Following the adoption of the corporate governance model whereby management and control functions are entrusted respectively to a Board of Directors and to an Audit Committee established within the Board itself, the Board of Directors is made up of 15 Directors, of whom 4 make up the Audit Committee  Discover more on selection and composition  Composition  Chairman  Pietro Carlo Padoan  Chairman of the Board of Directors  Complete CV  Deputy Vice Chair  Elena Carletti  Deputy Vice Chair  Complete CV  Chief Executive Officer  Andrea Orcel  UniCredit Group CEO and Head Of Italy, Chairman UniCredit Foundation, Chairman of HypoVereinsbank - UniCredit Bank GmbH  Complete CV  Directors  Paola Bergamaschi  Director  Complete CV  Paola Camagni  Director  Complete CV  Vincenzo Cariello  Director</data>
    </edge>
