      <data key="e_quote">Thales   83 4      Governance and compensation      Composition of the Board of Directors         4.1            Composition of the Board of Directors       4.1.1 Principles governing the composition of the Board of Directors,            shareholders' agreement and the selection procedure for directors      The Company is a public limited company with a Board of Directors.                  In addition, the shareholders’ agreement states that the Chairman                                                                                          and Chief Executive Officer will be chosen based on a joint      Under the terms of the shareholders’ agreement between the Public                   proposal by the Public Sector and Dassault Aviation (or the      Sector and the Industrial Partner (Dassault Aviation), as published on              Chairman of the Board and the Chief Executive Officer if the      the AMF site, the Board of Directors is composed of 16 directors,                   functions are separated with the joint approval of the two      14 of whom are appointed by the Annual General Meeting (or by                       shareholders) and that at least one director representing each of the      decree), and 2 of whom are appointed by the trade unions                            parties must sit on each of the Committees of the Board.      representing employees, in accordance with law (Article      L. 225-27-1 and following of the French Commercial Code) and the                    In practice, the selection of candidates for Board membership is carried      Articles of association (Article 10).                                               out in accordance with the requirements for balanced representation of                                                                                          men and women on boards of directors set out in law No. 2011-103      Of the 14 seats filled upon decisions of the shareholders or by decree:             of January 27, 2011 (known as the “Copé-Zimmerman” law) and in      • four are occupied by “External directors” selected jointly by the                 the transposition of Directive (EU) No. 2022/2381 of November 23,        Public Sector and Dassault Aviation (1);                                          2022 (known as “Women on Boards”), and in the light of the Board’s      • one is occupied by the employee shareholder representative (2);                   diversity objectives and skills matrix, as well as the expertise and                                                                                          experience of the directors (see section 4.1.3 below); in any case, all      • five are proposed to the Annual General Meeting by the Public                                                                                          of the above will be considered in compliance with the rules of the        Sector or appointed by decree (3); and                                                                                          shareholders’ agreement mentioned above.      • four are proposed to the Annual General Meeting by        Dassault Aviation.                                                                The 2014 Annual General Meeting set the term of office for                                                                                          directors at four years.          (1)   Their candidacy is examined beforehand by the Governance and Compensation Committee, as indicated in section 4.2.3.2 b) below.      (2)   This candidacy is submitted to the Annual General Meeting in accordance with the French Commercial Code and the Articles of Association (Article 10).      (3)   In accordance with Article 4-I of Ordinance No. 2014-948, the French State appoints its representative to the Board directly by decree, without consulting the            Annual General Meeting.This has been the case since the French State took over TSA’s shares from EPIC Bpifrance on September 5, 2023. By decree dated            January 29, 2024, Mr. Alexis Zajdenweber succeeded Mr. Emmanuel Moulin as the State’s new representative on the Board of Directors.   84   Thales – 2025 Universal Registration Document                                                                                                                Governance and compensation                                                                                                                                 Composition of the Board of Directors    4.1.2 Composition of the Board as of December 31, 2025 a) Summary presentation (in accordance with Appendix III of the Afep-Medef code)  Directors at December 31, 2025                                Age         Gender           Nationality                  Number of              Number of terms of office                                                                                                                        Thales shares                        held in other                                                                                                                                                        listed companies  Appointed by the Annual General Meeting (13)  or by decree (1) (a)  On the proposal of the Public Sector (5)  Patrice Caine,  Chairman and Chief Executive Officer</data>
