      <data key="e_source_url">https://www.unicreditgroup.eu/en/governance/governance-bodies/board-of-directors.html</data>
      <data key="e_quote">UniCredit  Consent to the use of cookies  This website uses technical, analytics and profiling Cookies, also installed by third parties (so called Third-Party Cookies).  Profiling Cookies are used in order to offer you advertising messages in line with your preferences ; their installation requires your prior consent .  Further information on the cookies installed through this website are available by accessing the Cookie Policy , always available on this website.  By clicking on the X at the top right, your navigation will continue without profiling cookies.  ACCEPT ALL COOKIES  MORE INFO  Messaggio  Skip to:  Secondary Menu Content Footer  Close Hamburger  MAGAZINE  FAQ  CALENDAR  WORLDWIDE  EN  Language  ITALIANO  ENGLISH  DEUTSCH --&gt;  BACK  Strategy  About us  Governance  Investors  Press &amp; Media  Careers  Strategy  With UniCredit Unlimited, we are stepping into a new era. One defined by bold ambition and a fundamental shift in how a European bank operates.  Overview Page Strategy  Our Purpose  Our Business  Our Business  Overview Page Our Business  Our approach to business  Client Solutions  Our Investment Insights  Corporate Clients  Retail, Private and Wealth Management  Digital &amp; Data  Longevity  Our Financial Ambition  Our Structural Advantages  About us  UniCredit is a leading pan-European bank providing best-in-class solutions and services across Italy, Germany, Austria and Central &amp; Eastern Europe. Our vision is to be the Bank for Europe's Future, driven by our purpose to Empower Communities to Progress.  Overview Page About us  Organisational structure  Organisational structure  Overview Page Organisational structure  Controlled companies  Our Culture &amp; Values  ESG and Sustainability  ESG and Sustainability  Overview Page ESG and Sustainability  Environmental  Social  Governance  Sustainability Reporting  ESG Day  Awards and Recognitions  Awards and Recognitions  Overview Page Awards and Recognitions  Group  Diversity, Equity and Inclusion  Diversity, Equity and Inclusion  Overview Page Diversity, Equity and Inclusion  DE&amp;I Framework: promoting diversity and inclusion  Gender equality and inclusion in the workplace  Inclusive culture and inclusion at work  Beyond March 8, together  Art, Music and Sport  Art, Music and Sport  Overview Page Art, Music and Sport  Art  Music  Sport  ESG Sustainability Policies and Ratings  Read More  Governance  UniCredit is committed to the highest standards of corporate governance, ensuring transparency and accountability for all stakeholders.  Overview Page Governance  Our Governance System  Our Governance System  Overview Page Our Governance System  Articles of Association and Code of Ethics  Related Parties and Associated Persons  Shareholders  Shareholders  Overview Page Shareholders  Shareholders structure  Archive  FAQ  Corporate bodies  Corporate bodies  Overview Page Corporate bodies  Board of Directors  Selection process and composition  Independence  Board Committees  Audit Committee  Activities &amp; meetings attendance  Our internal control systems  Management  Remuneration  Remuneration  Overview Page Remuneration  Governance &amp; Compliance  Incentive systems  Directors and Auditors compensation  Internal Dealings  Internal Dealings  Overview Page Internal Dealings  Transactions  Individual Holdings  Investors  Access UniCredit’s latest financial information, shared transparently and promptly with the investor community.  Overview Page Investors  Financial reporting  Financial reporting  Overview Page Financial reporting  Financial Reports  Financial highlights  Third pillar of Basel 2 and Basel 3  Conferences &amp; Other Presentations  Financial press releases  Financial calendar  Group Results  Equity investors  Equity investors  Overview Page Equity investors  Share price  Share information  Dividends  Shareholders structure  Equity analysts  Consensus  Debt investors  Debt investors  Overview Page Debt investors  Fixed income and ESG presentations  Funding programmes and prospectuses  Credit Ratings  Fixed income analysts  ESG investors  Retail investors  Contacts  Alerts  Press &amp; Media  This section provides access to UniCredit’s press releases, media resources and corporate materials, offering journalists and industry professionals up-to-date information on the Group.  Overview Page Press &amp; Media  Press Releases  News  Social Media  Podcasts  Podcasts  Overview Page Podcasts  Conversations Unlocked  Press Kit  Events Calendar  Contacts  Careers  Find the latest job opportunities at UniCredit and explore how you can build your career within a leading pan-European bank.  Overview Page Careers  Well-being  Learning &amp; Growth  Compensation &amp; Benefits  Online Banking --&gt; Online Banking  MAGAZINE  FAQ  CALENDAR  WORLDWIDE  SEARCH  EN  Language  ITALIANO  ENGLISH  DEUTSCH --&gt;  Hamburger Menu  Online Banking --&gt; Online Banking  Search  Search  Home  Governance  Corporate bodies  Board of Directors  Share  Print  Send  --&gt;  Share this event on:  X  LinkedIn  --&gt;  Recomend this page  Thank you, we sent your recommendation to the desired recipient.  Sorry, this functionality is not available right now. Please try with this link . Thank you.  Sender:  Recipient (e-mail address):  Send  Back to Corporate Bodies  Board of Directors  Our Board of Directors can be made from a minimum of 9 up to a maximum of 19 members, of whom at least 3 - and, in any case, no more than 5 - make up the Audit Committee.  Directors' term in office is three financial years, unless a shorter term is established at the time of their appointment, and ends on the date of the Shareholders' Meeting called for the approval of the financial statements relating to the last financial year in which they are in office.  The Board of Directors currently in office was appointed by the ordinary Shareholders' Meeting on April 12, 2024 for the financial years 2024 - 2026, on the basis of a proportional representation mechanism ("voto di lista"), and its terms of office ends on the date of the Shareholders' Meeting called to approve the 2026 financial statements.  As regards the actions taken in recent years to strengthen our governance and align it with international best practices, improving the composition and functioning of the Board of Directors has been a fundamental commitment for our Group.  Board of Directors evolution  2017  2018  2019  2020  2021  2023  2024  Faculty to file its own list of candidates in the event of its renewal  Increase from 1 to 2 in the number of Directors appointed from the minority slates  Size of the Board of Directors reduced from 17 to 15, number of Vice Chairmen reduced from 3 to 1  Board's tenure equal to maximum 3 mandates  Increased diversity  Identified Digital &amp; Technology and Banking Business as the major competence areas to be developed within the Board  Size of the Board of Directors reduced from 15 to 14  Strengthen the Board of Directors' collective suitability through (i) broad coverage of financial services; (ii) exposure to international markets &amp; geographies; (iii) broad range of industrial &amp; digital expertise; (iv) increased diversity  Size of the Board of Directors reduced from 14 to 13  Size of the Board of Directors reduced from 13 to 12  Following the adoption of the corporate governance model whereby management and control functions are entrusted respectively to a Board of Directors and to an Audit Committee established within the Board itself, the Board of Directors is made up of 15 Directors, of whom 4 make up the Audit Committee  Discover more on selection and composition  Composition  Chairman  Pietro Carlo Padoan  Chairman of the Board of Directors</data>
    </edge>
