um of two             The Sustainability Committee gives advice on measures independent and non-executive members of the Board. The              which ensure the long-term sustainability of the Company Nomination Committee oversees the long-term succession               in its economic, social and environmental dimension and planning of the Board, establishes the principles and criteria       monitors the Company’s performance against selected for the selection of candidates to the Board, selects                external sustainability indexes. While the full Board approves candidates for election or re-election to the Board and              the Company’s Non-Financial Statement for submission to prepares a proposal for the Board’s decision. It is regularly        the Annual General Meeting, the Sustainability Committee supported by external search firms.                                  has oversight over the structure and content of the Company’s    The succession planning for the Board of Directors is             non-financial reporting. It reviews the Company’s response highly structured and seeks to ensure a balance of relevant          to climate change and other environmental issues, it ensures competencies and an appropriate diversity of its members.            the Company carries out human rights due diligence and The Nomination Committee regularly reviews the Company’s             reports on its most severe human rights risks, and it reviews skills and diversity grid (see 3.1. above) and ensures appropriate   the Company’s diversity and inclusion and employee health cognitive diversity. It ensures an appropriately wide net is         and well-being. It meets at least four times a year and as cast on key successions. The candidates to the Board must            frequently as necessary to fulfil its tasks. It keeps the Board possess the necessary profile, qualifications and experience         updated on the material issues affecting the long-term to discharge their duties. Newly appointed Board members             sustainability of the Group. receive an appropriate introduction to the business and affairs of the Company and the Group. If required, the               Audit Committee Nomination Committee arranges for further training.                  The Audit Committee consists of a Chair, who is    The Nomination Committee reviews, at least annually, the          an independent and non-executive member of the Board, independence of the members of the Board as well as their            and a minimum of two other non-executive members of outside mandates, and prepares the annual self-evaluation            the Board, excluding the CEO and any former member of the Board and its Committees. It meets as frequently              of the Executive Board. All members shall be independent. as necessary to fulfil its tasks and prepares the relevant           At least one member has to have recent and relevant financial in camera sessions of the Board of Directors.                        expertise, the others must be familiar with the issues of                                                                      accounting and audit. In discharging its responsibilities, the                                                                      Audit Committee has unrestricted access to the Company’s                                                                      management, books and records. The Audit Committee                                                                      supports the Board of Directors in its supervision of financial                                                                      controls through a direct link to the external auditors (EY)                                                                      and Nestlé Internal Audit (corporate internal auditors). It has                                                                      oversight over the accuracy of the Company’s financial and                                                                      non-financial reporting. It reviews management reports on                                                                      the Company’s risk management, as well as the Group’s                                                                      financial position, balance sheet and financial risk                                                                      management.     14                                                                                                   Corporate Governance Report 2025 Board of Directors     The Audit Committee’s main duties include the following: – to review, and challenge where necessary, the actions and   judgements of management, in relation to the Company’s   year-end financial accounts and where necessary interim   accounts; – to make recommendations to the Board of Directors   regarding the nomination of external auditors to be   appointed by the shareholders; – to discuss the audit procedures, including the proposed   scope and the results of the internal and external audits; – to keep itself regularly informed on important findings   of the audits and of their progress; – to oversee the quality of the internal and external auditing; – to present the conclusions on the approval of the Financial   Statements to the Board of Directors; – to review reports regarding internal controls, compliance,   fraud, enterprise risk management and the Group’s annual   risk assessment; – to oversee the accuracy of the Group’s non-financial   reporting; – to review management reports as the Company’s risk   management; – to review the Group’s balance sheet and financial risk   management.  The Audit Committee regularly reports to the Board on its findings and proposes appropriate actions. The responsibility for approving the annual Financial Statements and the Non- Financial Statement remains with the Board of Directors.     Corporate Governance Report 2025        