    <edge id="e2544" source="christel-heydemann" target="orange">
      <data key="e_predicate">employed_by</data>
      <data key="e_edge_class">occupational</data>
      <data key="e_role">board_member</data>
      <data key="e_grade">A</data>
      <data key="e_n_sources">1</data>
      <data key="e_doc_id">official-orange-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_doc_title">official-orange-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_doc_path">sources/official/orange-board-of-directors.txt</data>
      <data key="e_source_url">https://www.orange.com/en/our-group/our-governance/our-board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_quote">Orange and their partners use cookies (or equivalent technologies).  With your agreement, we and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on the link in the footer or in our Cookie policy on this website.  We and our partners process data for the following purposes: Analytics, Digital Accessibility, Personalised advertising and content, advertising and content measurement, audience research and services development, Precise geolocation data, and identification through device scanning, Store and/or access information on a device, Technical Cookies, User Feedback  View our 12 partners Customize Disagree Agree Skip to main content Orange Business All our sites Media library  ORA  14,45€  -0,14%  Confort+ FR EN Our Group Our impact Our expertise Our news Finance Press Careers Search on the website Homepage Our governance Our Board of directors Our Board of directors Our Board of Directors, shaping Orange’s future  The Board oversees all decisions tied to Orange’s major strategic, economic, social, financial, technological and environmental priorities. Medium-term direction for the Group is set through a strategic plan that is updated regularly. The CEO presents this plan to the Board, which then reviews and adopts it. The plan includes projected trends for key operational, social and financial indicators to ensure alignment with market developments.  The balance and stability of the Council  Bloc Exergue Item 15 members  make up Orange's Board of Directors.  Bloc Exergue Item 7 independent directors  ensuring a balance of power  Bloc Exergue Item 4 years  the term of office of each director  A balanced Board for effective governance  Orange’s Board of Directors brings together 15 members with varied backgrounds: seven independent directors, three representing the public sector, three representing employees and one representing employee shareholders (currently vacant). This diversity of experience and expertise ensures balance, independence and strong oversight. Each director serves a four-year term, in line with the bylaws updated at the Annual Shareholders’ Meeting on May 19, 2022.  Our commitment to the highest standards in governance  In corporate governance, Orange follows the recommendations of the Afep-Medef Code (“Corporate Governance Code for Listed Companies”) as revised in December 2022. This document can be viewed in the “Governance Documentation” section of our site and is also available on the Afep and Medef websites.  Orange’s Board ensures that the key pillars of our Trust the Future strategic plan are carried out effectively. It reviews the major milestones of the Group’s activity, including operational performance, quarterly results, half-year and annual accounts, budget, risk factors and sustainability status. It also determines the compensation of company directors and examines major strategic projects, including significant portfolio operations and long-term investments.  Board composition  Frédéric Sanchez Chairman of the Board, Independent Director  Christel Heydemann Chief Executive Officer, Director</data>
    </edge>
