    <edge id="e2596" source="flavio-cattaneo" target="enel">
      <data key="e_predicate">employed_by</data>
      <data key="e_edge_class">occupational</data>
      <data key="e_role">employed_by</data>
      <data key="e_grade">A</data>
      <data key="e_n_sources">2</data>
      <data key="e_doc_id">official-enel-board</data>
      <data key="e_doc_title">official-enel-board</data>
      <data key="e_doc_path">sources/official/enel-board.txt</data>
      <data key="e_source_url">https://www.enel.com/investors/governance/board-of-directors</data>
      <data key="e_quote">enel.com/investors/governance/board-of-directors TITLE: Board of Directors | Enel Group  Enel Group Group websites Enel Green Power Producing clean energy with renewable sources Enel Global Energy and Commodity Management Mitigating commodity trading risks at global scale Enel Open Innovability® A global ecosystem that leverages Innovability® to power the future Enel Global Procurement We maximize value creation through our relationships with suppliers Enel Foundation Knowledge platform for a clean energy world Enel Cuore We support the initiatives undertaken by NPOs Ethical Channel Providing ways to report violation of our policies Country websites Americas Argentina Brasil Chile Colombia Iberia Italy Mexico North America Follow us Facebook Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Instagram Skip to Main Content Company Media Investors Careers Enel Overview Strategy Financials Investing Sustainability Governance Governance Governance Board of Directors Board of Directors  The Board of Directors plays a central role in the Company's governance structure. Management of the Company is the exclusive responsibility of the Directors, who shall carry out the actions necessary to achieve the corporate purpose.  In line with the recommendations set forth by the Italian Corporate Governance Code, the Board of Directors approved in February 2021 specific Regulations, last update in July 2025, defining the role, composition and functioning of the Board itself, including the procedures for scheduling, convening and holding its meetings, as well as for drafting the relevant minutes. Furthermore, the Regulations of the Board of Directors set forth procedures for managing the information to be provided to Directors, also considering the role assigned in this respect to the Chairman of the Board of Directors and to the Secretary of the Board itself, as well as confidentiality obligations related to information received in connection with Board meetings. Finally, specific provisions are laid down with regard to the self-evaluation process carried out by the Board of Directors, to the Board induction programme and to the contingency plan drawn up for the role of Chief Executive Officer.  The current Board of Directors was appointed by the Shareholders' Meeting of May 12, 2026 for a term of three financial years. The Board's mandate will therefore expire with the Shareholders' Meeting to be convened for the approval of the financial statements for the year ending December 31, 2028.  Paolo Scaroni Chairman (1) Discover more Flavio Cattaneo Chief Executive Officer</data>
    </edge>
