ion, please refer to the Board Regulations and Committee Charters at www.nestle.com/investors/corporate-governance/boardcommittees     Corporate Governance Report 2025                                                                                                                              17 Board of Directors         The Audit Committee reviews the financial performance             The role of Nestlé Internal Audit is to enhance and protect and assesses the effectiveness of the internal and external       organizational value by providing risk-based and objective audit processes as well as the internal risk management           assurance, advice and insight, contributing to the continuous organization and processes. It regularly performs a review        improvement of the Company’s risk management and control of the assets and liabilities management by the Company’s         systems. Nestlé Internal Audit assesses the reliability of treasury, pensions and insurance departments with the             financial and operational information, the effectiveness of Chief Financial Officer and the Head of Treasury, Pensions &amp;      controls and processes for compliance with internal, legal, Insurance being present. It has oversight over the accuracy of    regulatory and statutory requirements. Findings are the financial and non-financial reporting. It reviews reports     communicated in the form of an audit report, which is shared on the Company’s internal control, compliance and risk            with management and the Audit Committee. management processes. It has complete and unrestricted                The Head of Nestlé Internal Audit reports administratively access to the Company’s management, books and records             to the Chief Financial Officer and has a functional reporting and may obtain any information it requires from the               line to the Chair of the Audit Committee. He reports at all the appropriate services. Members of the Executive Board and          Audit Committee meetings, has direct access to the Chair other senior management, in particular the Heads of Group         of the Audit Committee and regularly meets with him for Accounting &amp; Reporting, Internal Audit and Legal and              interim updates. The Audit Committee regularly receives Compliance, attend the Audit Committee meetings, except           a report on the results of the internal auditors’ work that is for certain in camera sessions.                                   also provided to the Chair of the Board of Directors, Executive     The Nomination Committee leads the succession planning        Board members and other stakeholders. It reviews and for the Board of Directors.                                       monitors management’s responsiveness to internal audit     The Sustainability Committee reviews reports on measures      findings and recommendations. In case of major findings, that ensure the long-term sustainability of the Company in its    a follow-up audit is planned to ensure proper remediation. economic, social and environmental dimension. It has oversight        Group Risk Management provides assistance to all over the structure and content of the non-financial reporting     corporate entities with regard to risk management. Group and monitors the Company’s performance against selected           Risk Services provides assistance to all corporate entities external sustainability indexes. It oversees the Company’s        with regard to loss prevention, claims handling and response to climate change, its human rights program and          insurance. Enterprise Risk Management (ERM) is a process human capital management. Members of management,                  applied across the Group, designed to identify potential in particular the CEO, the Heads of Public Affairs and of Legal   events that may affect the Group’s achievement of its and Compliance, may attend the meetings.                          strategic objectives and support the Group to ensure it acts     The Compensation Committee reviews the Company’s              in accordance with external regulations and internal policies. compensation system and principles. The Head of Human             It supports Nestlé’s management to raise risk awareness Resources may attend the meetings, except when questions          and to anticipate emerging risks, as well as the process of compensation for Executive Board members are                   of identifying appropriate mitigation actions. deliberated.                                                          The Nestlé Group adopts a dual approach using “Top-     Additional information and control instruments include        Down” and “Bottom-Up” assessments. The “Top-Down” the external auditors, Ernst &amp; Young Ltd, auditors of             assessment occurs annually and focuses on the Group’s Nestlé S.A. and of the Consolidated Financial Statements          global risks. A “Bottom‑Up” assessment occurs in parallel, of the Nestlé Group, who conduct their audit in compliance        resulting in the aggregation of individual assessments by with Swiss law and in accordance with Swiss Auditing              all Markets, Regionally and Globally Managed Businesses. Standards and International Standards on Auditing, and the            Additionally, Nestlé engages with external stakeholders Nestlé Internal Audit function.                                   to better understand the issues that are of most concern to     Nestlé Internal Audit comprises an organization of one        them. For each issue, the materiality matrix (please refer to Center Team and eight regional units of auditors covering         the Non-Financial Statement) rates the degree of stakeholder all the businesses (i.e. head offices, factories, distribution    concern and potential business impact. centers and business units) worldwide, completing audit               Group ERM combines the output of the “Top-Down” assignments on the basis of the annual internal audit plan        assessment, the “Bottom-Up” assessments and the external based on an independent risk assessment that is approved          stakeholder assessments which is presented annually to the by the Audit Committee.                                           Executive Board. The Annual Risk Report is reviewed by the   18                                                                                                Corporate Governance Report 2025 Board of Directors     Audit Committee, and material risks are reviewed by the Board of Directors on an annual basis.    For more information on the Nestlé Group Enterprise Risk Management, please refer to page 52 of the Annual Review 2025.    Group Compliance and other risk- and control-related functions provide additional guidance and oversight. Risk and compliance activities are coordinated through the Group Compliance Committee to ensure a holistic, entity-wide approach. The Chief Compliance Officer has direct access to the Chair of the Audit Committee. The Audit Committee is provided yearly with the Group Compliance Report, a comprehensive documentation of the Company’s compliance framework, systems, activities and improvement actions pursued by the various functions. It includes a summary of the feedback received on the Group’s integrity reporting system as well as the functional third-party compliance audits (CARE). The Group Compliance Report is also reviewed by the Board of Directors.    For more information on the Group’s Governance and Compliance, please refer to pages 59 and 64 of the Annual Review 2025.     Corporate Governance Report 2025                              19 Executive Board   4.      Executive Board 4.1     Members of the Executive Board    Name                                       Year of birth         Nationality          Education/current function Philipp Navratil                           1976                  Swiss/               Business Adm